u Vuggepalli"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:58:18.403Z","repositoryId":1234652119,"sha":"fc4b385d364d1334370326767f9a91340945057f"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:58:18.403Z","raw":[{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/b56d2a6aecc2d8e5c31daf4a9217a68b6c241617/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T03:17:30Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T03:17:30Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"message":"feat(ports): per-port RX/TX byte counters end-to-end\n\nPortState/PortStateOut gain optional rx_bytes/tx_bytes (None = driver exposes\nno counters, distinct from 0). The SwOS driver reads stats.b in get_ports and\nsets 64-bit RX/TX bytes per port (best-effort: a stats failure leaves them\nNone, port list still returns). Frontend Port model + mapPort carry them; the\nport detail panel shows RX/TX rows when present (formatBytes helper). OpenAPI\ntypes regenerated. Live-validated on the CSS326 (Port2 = 71.2 GB RX).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ec91ab5e1603731b291adde1aa8c15ad1825a3ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/trees/ec91ab5e1603731b291adde1aa8c15ad1825a3ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/commits/b56d2a6aecc2d8e5c31daf4a9217a68b6c241617","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/b56d2a6aecc2d8e5c31daf4a9217a68b6c241617","node_id":"C_kwDOSZdL19oAKGI1NmQyYTZhZWNjMmQ4ZTVjMzFkYWY0YTkyMTdhNjhiNmMyNDE2MTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/d72bd1fa46ab7d71a90bcb3ee5829e5275640c5a","sha":"d72bd1fa46ab7d71a90bcb3ee5829e5275640c5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/d72bd1fa46ab7d71a90bcb3ee5829e5275640c5a"}],"sha":"b56d2a6aecc2d8e5c31daf4a9217a68b6c241617","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/b56d2a6aecc2d8e5c31daf4a9217a68b6c241617"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/d72bd1fa46ab7d71a90bcb3ee5829e5275640c5a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T03:08:52Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T03:08:52Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"message":"feat(ui): filter the per-device port list by BMC / VLAN\n\nPortStrip gains a filter bar: text search (matches BMC IP, name, description),\na ''Has BMC'' toggle (ports with a BMC IP), and untagged/tagged VLAN dropdowns\npopulated from the VLANs actually present on the device. Counts + the empty\nstate reflect the active filter; Clear resets all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7c697af9725b92fac8fdbdd142da2bf5db6167c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/trees/7c697af9725b92fac8fdbdd142da2bf5db6167c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/commits/d72bd1fa46ab7d71a90bcb3ee5829e5275640c5a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/d72bd1fa46ab7d71a90bcb3ee5829e5275640c5a","node_id":"C_kwDOSZdL19oAKGQ3MmJkMWZhNDZhYjdkNzFhOTBiY2IzZWU1ODI5ZTUyNzU2NDBjNWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/28bbf6857b2ef4d10c25e7a8194ce2e601f2dbc8","sha":"28bbf6857b2ef4d10c25e7a8194ce2e601f2dbc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/28bbf6857b2ef4d10c25e7a8194ce2e601f2dbc8"}],"sha":"d72bd1fa46ab7d71a90bcb3ee5829e5275640c5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/d72bd1fa46ab7d71a90bcb3ee5829e5275640c5a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/28bbf6857b2ef4d10c25e7a8194ce2e601f2dbc8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T03:05:57Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T03:05:57Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"message":"feat(swos): add Errors table to Diagnostics counters\n\nThird stats.b table alongside counters + histogram: RX FCS/align/overflow/\nfragments + TX collisions (rfcs/rae/rov/fr/tcl). Keys confirmed present and\nlive-validated on a CSS326 (SFP1 shows 7 FCS errors, rest zero on healthy links).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"22e861cbc6a89b6eda602023618235f1081452d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/trees/22e861cbc6a89b6eda602023618235f1081452d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/commits/28bbf6857b2ef4d10c25e7a8194ce2e601f2dbc8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/28bbf6857b2ef4d10c25e7a8194ce2e601f2dbc8","node_id":"C_kwDOSZdL19oAKDI4YmJmNjg1N2IyZWY0ZDEwYzI1ZTdhODE5NGNlMmU2MDFmMmRiYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/a340b314f34debd0a7ba77c6033ecb8f2d4d3b6c","sha":"a340b314f34debd0a7ba77c6033ecb8f2d4d3b6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/a340b314f34debd0a7ba77c6033ecb8f2d4d3b6c"}],"sha":"28bbf6857b2ef4d10c25e7a8194ce2e601f2dbc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/28bbf6857b2ef4d10c25e7a8194ce2e601f2dbc8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/a340b314f34debd0a7ba77c6033ecb8f2d4d3b6c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T02:55:56Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T02:55:56Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"message":"feat(swos): MAC/host table + Diagnostics counters & histogram\n\nThe device in the field is SwOS, not RouterOS — the prior MikroTik reads\n(mikrotik.py) didn''t apply to it. SwOS get_system_info now reads the dynamic\nhost table (/!dhost.b: adr/vid/prt, prt a 0-based port index) so the System\ntab MAC table populates. get_protocol_detail(''Counters'') reads /stats.b for\nper-port traffic counters (64-bit rb/rbh, tb/tbh bytes; rtp/ttp packets —\nverified live to equal unicast+broadcast+multicast) plus the RMON packet-size\nhistogram (p64..p1k). All endpoints/fields grounded against MikroTik docs and\nLIVE-VALIDATED against a CSS326-24G-2S+ (SwOS 2.18): 82 real hosts, real\ncounters. Fixtures captured from that box.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5b459eac1d04d2cdc48822fe5b76f64dbe1073f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/trees/5b459eac1d04d2cdc48822fe5b76f64dbe1073f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/commits/a340b314f34debd0a7ba77c6033ecb8f2d4d3b6c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/a340b314f34debd0a7ba77c6033ecb8f2d4d3b6c","node_id":"C_kwDOSZdL19oAKGEzNDBiMzE0ZjM0ZGViZDBhN2JhNzdjNjAzM2VjYjhmMmQ0ZDNiNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/acca3aed1e7ad8b2b5c59ac1d8acdbda4170e032","sha":"acca3aed1e7ad8b2b5c59ac1d8acdbda4170e032","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/acca3aed1e7ad8b2b5c59ac1d8acdbda4170e032"}],"sha":"a340b314f34debd0a7ba77c6033ecb8f2d4d3b6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/a340b314f34debd0a7ba77c6033ecb8f2d4d3b6c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/acca3aed1e7ad8b2b5c59ac1d8acdbda4170e032/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T00:12:16Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T00:12:16Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"message":"fix(ui): invalid Button kind ''secondary'' on config Retry → ''outline''\n\ntsc -b (build mode, used by vite build) caught what tsc --noEmit missed:\nButton''s kind union has no ''secondary''. Retry button now uses ''outline''.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"49beb42f0c43ecd889f24e1aed0238107bd1c49a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/trees/49beb42f0c43ecd889f24e1aed0238107bd1c49a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/commits/acca3aed1e7ad8b2b5c59ac1d8acdbda4170e032","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/acca3aed1e7ad8b2b5c59ac1d8acdbda4170e032","node_id":"C_kwDOSZdL19oAKGFjY2EzYWVkMWU3YWQ4YjJiNWM1OWFjMWQ4YWNkYmRhNDE3MGUwMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/18473c2f9d1cf1a2fb3b2b9d84921f63577d579f","sha":"18473c2f9d1cf1a2fb3b2b9d84921f63577d579f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/18473c2f9d1cf1a2fb3b2b9d84921f63577d579f"}],"sha":"acca3aed1e7ad8b2b5c59ac1d8acdbda4170e032","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/acca3aed1e7ad8b2b5c59ac1d8acdbda4170e032"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/18473c2f9d1cf1a2fb3b2b9d84921f63577d579f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T00:07:43Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T00:07:43Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"message":"feat(ui): real running-config view + delete-request controls\n\nRunning config: DeviceConfigView fetched a client-side synthesis from the\nport list (VLANs only). Now wired to GET /api/devices/{id}/config (full\ndevice dump) with real Backup-now and backup diff, loading/error states.\n\nDelete requests: Delete button + confirm in both the queue (admin) and mine\n(owner) views, gated to non-applied states; new ''cancelled'' status in the\nmodel + StatusBadge. cancelRequest client + useCancelRequest hook.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f9409fd84778eb4a10ed2cddc9914e4ad9ba2c61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/trees/f9409fd84778eb4a10ed2cddc9914e4ad9ba2c61"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/commits/18473c2f9d1cf1a2fb3b2b9d84921f63577d579f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/18473c2f9d1cf1a2fb3b2b9d84921f63577d579f","node_id":"C_kwDOSZdL19oAKDE4NDczYzJmOWQxY2YxYTJmYjNiMmI5ZDg0OTIxZjYzNTc3ZDU3OWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/0fa1b0191551161a4a182599930fc2f28dedda90","sha":"0fa1b0191551161a4a182599930fc2f28dedda90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/0fa1b0191551161a4a182599930fc2f28dedda90"}],"sha":"18473c2f9d1cf1a2fb3b2b9d84921f63577d579f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/18473c2f9d1cf1a2fb3b2b9d84921f63577d579f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/0fa1b0191551161a4a182599930fc2f28dedda90/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T00:07:43Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T00:07:43Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"message":"feat(mikrotik): MAC table + Diagnostics (counters/ARP/routing) reads\n\nget_system_info now reads the bridge host table (/interface/bridge/host) so\nthe System tab MAC table populates for RouterOS — previously it returned\nempty (mac_supported=false). Adds get_protocol_detail for the Diagnostics\nslugs Counters (/interface, humanized byte counters), ARP (/ip/arp) and\nRouting (/ip/route, v7 immediate-gw). All REST field names grounded against\nMikroTik docs; values string-coerced (REST returns everything as strings).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fa55f9ae4f0e8ee8cf1358c88a025ae3a4b960ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/trees/fa55f9ae4f0e8ee8cf1358c88a025ae3a4b960ff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/commits/0fa1b0191551161a4a182599930fc2f28dedda90","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/0fa1b0191551161a4a182599930fc2f28dedda90","node_id":"C_kwDOSZdL19oAKDBmYTFiMDE5MTU1MTE2MWE0YTE4MjU5OTkzMGZjMmYyOGRlZGRhOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/06d4c3a114ef5961240a687e72d77c44c361852c","sha":"06d4c3a114ef5961240a687e72d77c44c361852c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/06d4c3a114ef5961240a687e72d77c44c361852c"}],"sha":"0fa1b0191551161a4a182599930fc2f28dedda90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/0fa1b0191551161a4a182599930fc2f28dedda90"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/06d4c3a114ef5961240a687e72d77c44c361852c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T00:07:31Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T00:07:31Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"message":"feat(requests): soft-cancel (delete) for owner + admin\n\nDELETE /api/requests/{id} withdraws a non-applied request: new terminal\nCANCELLED status, owner-or-admin authz (404 for a foreign id, no existence\nleak), 409 for applying/applied/awaiting_confirm/reverted. The row + its\nevent history are retained (compliance trail) — one cancelled transition is\nappended, never a hard delete.\n\nDialect-aware migration: PostgreSQL ALTER TYPE ... ADD VALUE (also backfills\nneeds_revision, never migrated to the PG enum); no-op on SQLite where status\nis a plain string column.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9c08ea742c7a87b6876abb4215b23c4d061844be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/trees/9c08ea742c7a87b6876abb4215b23c4d061844be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/commits/06d4c3a114ef5961240a687e72d77c44c361852c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/06d4c3a114ef5961240a687e72d77c44c361852c","node_id":"C_kwDOSZdL19oAKDA2ZDRjM2ExMTRlZjU5NjEyNDBhNjg3ZTcyZDc3YzQ0YzM2MTg1MmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/612331a148c24fced87e4fb78dbf94b85b194332","sha":"612331a148c24fced87e4fb78dbf94b85b194332","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/612331a148c24fced87e4fb78dbf94b85b194332"}],"sha":"06d4c3a114ef5961240a687e72d77c44c361852c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/06d4c3a114ef5961240a687e72d77c44c361852c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/612331a148c24fced87e4fb78dbf94b85b194332/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-11T19:10:56Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-11T19:10:56Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"message":"chore: remove dead code identified by knip/vulture sweep\n\nBackend (src/):\n- Remove _has_child() from drivers/pica8.py — defined but never called anywhere\n  in src/ or tests/ after the _clear_vlan_xml removal refactor\n- Remove _clear_for_tests() from drivers/registry.py — test-only helper with\n  zero call-sites in src/ or tests/\n- Remove SnmpClient.bulk_get() from _lib/transport/snmp_client.py — method\n  implemented but never invoked anywhere; multiget is used directly via walk()\n\nFrontend (frontend/src/):\n- Remove useConfirmRequest hook from api/queries.ts — exported mutation hook\n  with no import-site anywhere in the codebase (the underlying\n  api.confirmRequest() function in realClient.ts is kept)\n- Unexport VLAN_ZONES from lib/vlan.ts — only used internally by vlanZone();\n  no external consumer imports it\n- Unexport toEpochMs/toPlatform from api/mappers.ts — module-private helpers\n  used only within mappers.ts; export was unnecessary\n- Unexport Skeleton from shared/Skeleton.tsx — used only internally by\n  SkeletonList in the same file; only SkeletonList is imported externally\n- Remove DeviceOut/PortStateOut re-aliases from api/schema.ts — realClient.ts\n  redeclares them inline from schema.gen.ts; these re-exports had zero consumers\n- Remove unused type re-exports (ConfirmOnboardResult, CreateRequestInput,\n  DiscoverResult, LoginResult, TestConnectionResult, ApiError) from api/index.ts\n  barrel — nothing imports them from @/api; underlying types/class kept in place\n\nGate: backend 569 passed, frontend 74 passed, ruff+pyright 0 errors, tsc+eslint clean","tree":{"sha":"e4ded14bafa191404d25924333b13de7d58a400f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/trees/e4ded14bafa191404d25924333b13de7d58a400f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/commits/612331a148c24fced87e4fb78dbf94b85b194332","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/612331a148c24fced87e4fb78dbf94b85b194332","node_id":"C_kwDOSZdL19oAKDYxMjMzMWExNDhjMjRmY2VkODdlNGZiNzhkYmY5NGI4NWIxOTQzMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/92a65c5ce187a5e33dbf70465b4323c257588307","sha":"92a65c5ce187a5e33dbf70465b4323c257588307","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/92a65c5ce187a5e33dbf70465b4323c257588307"}],"sha":"612331a148c24fced87e4fb78dbf94b85b194332","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/612331a148c24fced87e4fb78dbf94b85b194332"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/92a65c5ce187a5e33dbf70465b4323c257588307/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-11T18:24:31Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-11T18:24:31Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"message":"feat: LACP/LAG read enrichment + DISABLED write scaffold; RFC 1123 hostname validation\n\nLACP / LAG\n- Read enrichment (real, usable): pica8 _parse_l3_interfaces_xml now surfaces\n  LAG member ports (forward <member> list AND xorplus reverse-pointer via\n  ether-options) plus LACP enable/mode/rate in the L3Interface.detail field;\n  _detail_lacp now surfaces system-priority and per-interface fast/slow rate.\n  All best-effort — never crashes on an absent field. Arista/Cisco have no\n  cheap LAG read (no get_l3_interfaces); MikroTik bond members would need an\n  extra API+join, so left as-is.\n- Write scaffold (DISABLED — NOT a live path): new LagChange DTO (validated:\n  RFC-clean name, member list, lacp mode/rate, system-priority) and an abstract\n  render_lag_change on the Driver ABC whose default raises NotSupported. NO\n  concrete driver implements it; NO _kind=\"lag\" apply branch or endpoint exists.\n  Contract test asserts EVERY driver raises NotSupported for a LAG write.\n  Rationale: a Northbound trunk-VLAN write authored-from-docs and never\n  live-validated corrupted production Pica8 leaf-02; a LAG write touches bond\n  membership + LACP on a live uplink, so it ships disabled until lab-validated.\n\nValidation gaps closed\n- Device name: RFC 1123 hostname validator on DeviceCreateIn.name (<=253,\n  labels 1..63 alnum+hyphen, no leading/trailing hyphen, case-insensitive).\n  ConnectionTestIn/DiscoverIn carry no name field. Existing names all valid.\n- Site name: it is a human display label (slug is the identifier), so spaces/\n  punctuation stay legal; hardened only against control chars / CR-LF.\n- Frontend: isPlausibleHostname in src/lib/format.ts + inline aria-invalid/\n  text-danger error on the wizard device-name field and the step-2 gate.\n- MAC audit: every mac field is output/read-only (PortState/PortOut/MacEntry/\n  base_mac); no MAC input field exists — nothing to validate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"29ea72b4ae428f7de7d88e21720066852ccfdb40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/trees/29ea72b4ae428f7de7d88e21720066852ccfdb40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/commits/92a65c5ce187a5e33dbf70465b4323c257588307","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/92a65c5ce187a5e33dbf70465b4323c257588307","node_id":"C_kwDOSZdL19oAKDkyYTY1YzVjZTE4N2E1ZTMzZGJmNzA0NjViNDMyM2MyNTc1ODgzMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/6185f343bb02c57dc15c0d2fa482459bc1e861ac","sha":"6185f343bb02c57dc15c0d2fa482459bc1e861ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/6185f343bb02c57dc15c0d2fa482459bc1e861ac"}],"sha":"92a65c5ce187a5e33dbf70465b4323c257588307","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/92a65c5ce187a5e33dbf70465b4323c257588307"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/6185f343bb02c57dc15c0d2fa482459bc1e861ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-11T17:54:30Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-11T17:54:30Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"message":"fix(validation): RFC-compliant IP + email validation across backend and frontend\n\nReplace length-only / hand-rolled checks at the DTO and form boundaries with\nbattle-tested, RFC-compliant validators.\n\nBackend (Python stdlib ipaddress + Pydantic EmailStr):\n- device.py: add IPv4/IPv6 address validation to mgmt_ip on ConnectionTestIn\n  (inherited by DiscoverIn) and DeviceCreateIn — previously length-only, no\n  format check. Uses ipaddress.ip_address (address, not CIDR).\n- driver.py PortChange.bmc_ip and port.py PortMetadataPatchIn.bmc_ip: add\n  optional IP-address validation (ipaddress.ip_address); empty/None still\n  allowed to clear/unset.\n- auth.py: RegisterRequest.email and UserCreate.email now use Pydantic v2\n  EmailStr (RFC 5322), backed by the email-validator package (added to\n  pyproject dependencies).\n\nFrontend (ipaddr.js, already RFC-compliant):\n- format.ts: replace hand-rolled isPlausibleIp / isPlausibleCidr /\n  isPlausibleArea with ipaddr.js-backed implementations. isPlausibleIp uses\n  IPv4.isValid and additionally rejects leading-zero octets to match the\n  Python backend; isPlausibleCidr uses parseCIDR (v4+v6); isPlausibleArea is\n  integer-or-IP.\n- L3Form.tsx: inline CIDR validation on the IP field + JS-enforced VLAN\n  (1–4094) and MTU (64–16360) ranges; disabled submit + red error spans.\n- OspfForm.tsx: inline router-id (IP) and area (int/dotted-quad) validation +\n  JS-enforced cost (1–65535); disabled submit + red error spans.\n- RequestModal.tsx BMC field already gated via isPlausibleIp (now lib-backed).\n- Declare ipaddr.js as a direct dependency in package.json/lockfile.\n\nTests:\n- tests/schemas/test_ip_email_validation.py: garbage/CIDR mgmt_ip + bmc_ip\n  rejected, valid v4 AND v6 accepted, empty bmc_ip allowed, malformed email\n  rejected, valid email accepted.\n- frontend/src/lib/format.test.ts: isPlausibleIp rejects 01.02.03.04 and\n  999.1.1.1, accepts 8.8.8.8; isPlausibleCidr accepts v4+v6 with prefix,\n  rejects bare address and garbage; isPlausibleArea accepts 0 / 0.0.0.0,\n  rejects non-numeric.","tree":{"sha":"4fc7d2b7723e04142a2d5195bd99be27f9b1d633","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/trees/4fc7d2b7723e04142a2d5195bd99be27f9b1d633"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/commits/6185f343bb02c57dc15c0d2fa482459bc1e861ac","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/6185f343bb02c57dc15c0d2fa482459bc1e861ac","node_id":"C_kwDOSZdL19oAKDYxODVmMzQzYmIwMmM1N2RjMTVjMGQyZmE0ODI0NTliYzFlODYxYWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/476147ab10e6bc0c6a1814a771952370d512fd5d","sha":"476147ab10e6bc0c6a1814a771952370d512fd5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/476147ab10e6bc0c6a1814a771952370d512fd5d"}],"sha":"6185f343bb02c57dc15c0d2fa482459bc1e861ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/6185f343bb02c57dc15c0d2fa482459bc1e861ac"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/476147ab10e6bc0c6a1814a771952370d512fd5d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-11T16:08:47Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-11T16:08:47Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"message":"fix(pica8): disable corrupting trunk tagged-VLAN write; harden candidate hygiene\n\nIncident: on a live Pica8/xorplus leaf (leaf-02) a trunk tagged-VLAN member\nwrite corrupted the switch''s NETCONF candidate. pica_netconf crashed processing\nthe staged deletion (\"Failed to merge deletions from rtrmgr\", exit status 1),\nleaving an orphaned delete in xorp_rtrmgr that BLOCKED ALL COMMITS on the switch.\n\nDefect (three compounding root causes):\n- render_change used a two-phase \"clear-then-set\" for trunk tagged-VLAN writes:\n  phase 1 (_clear_vlan_xml) emitted a standalone `<vlan> operation=\"remove\">` to\n  wipe the port''s whole <vlan> subtree before re-adding members.\n- apply_change only switched to default-operation=\"none\" when the payload string\n  contained operation=\"delete\" — the clear used operation=\"remove\", so the\n  destructive remove ran under the WRONG default-operation (implicit merge).\n- nothing guaranteed a candidate discard around the apply, so a partially-staged\n  edit could linger in PicOS''s shared, persistent candidate.\n\nFix:\n1. render_change now REFUSES a trunk tagged-VLAN member change, raising the\n   driver layer''s standard NotSupported (DriverError subclass, reused — the same\n   exception mikrotik raises for its unsupported trunk path) with a clear message\n   pointing at the device vendor UI. Access-mode / single untagged-VLAN /\n   description / mtu / enabled writes are unaffected.\n2. _clear_vlan_xml is removed entirely (replaced by an incident note); no apply\n   path can stage a destructive vlan-members remove/delete any more.\n3. apply_change brackets discard_changes() on BOTH entry AND a finally so every\n   exit (success, edit/commit/verify failure) leaves the shared candidate clean.\n   The operation-attr/default-operation dispatch now trips on BOTH \"delete\" and\n   \"remove\", closing the mismatch that let the leaf-02 remove run under merge.\n\nTests: render_change refuses the trunk tagged-VLAN path (explicit + inferred\nmode); apply brackets discard on entry and exit; a destructive remove/delete is\nstaged under default-operation=\"none\". 59 pica8 tests pass; full suite 496 passed\n/ 1 skipped (live SSH). No device, deploy, or DB touched.","tree":{"sha":"0bf964e31a46c97f44aa057481af64a897fc2a98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/trees/0bf964e31a46c97f44aa057481af64a897fc2a98"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/commits/476147ab10e6bc0c6a1814a771952370d512fd5d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/476147ab10e6bc0c6a1814a771952370d512fd5d","node_id":"C_kwDOSZdL19oAKDQ3NjE0N2FiMTBlNmJjMGM2YTE4MTRhNzcxOTUyMzcwZDUxMmZkNWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/e2236db818cd4a486afd956c62191787dfb312b1","sha":"e2236db818cd4a486afd956c62191787dfb312b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/e2236db818cd4a486afd956c62191787dfb312b1"}],"sha":"476147ab10e6bc0c6a1814a771952370d512fd5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/476147ab10e6bc0c6a1814a771952370d512fd5d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/e2236db818cd4a486afd956c62191787dfb312b1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T23:00:03Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T23:00:03Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"message":"fix(ui): gate the sidebar ''+'' (add device) to admins too\n\nMissed in 6706bce — the device-list sidebar had its own Plus button\nnavigating to /onboard, shown to every role.","tree":{"sha":"7f3216400ccd33a2a31f3bea5566d538ed1ce109","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/trees/7f3216400ccd33a2a31f3bea5566d538ed1ce109"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/commits/e2236db818cd4a486afd956c62191787dfb312b1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/e2236db818cd4a486afd956c62191787dfb312b1","node_id":"C_kwDOSZdL19oAKGUyMjM2ZGI4MThjZDRhNDg2YWZkOTU2YzYyMTkxNzg3ZGZiMzEyYjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/6706bcee9fea4fa85a42b4f1adc7dcb92a8d48ff","sha":"6706bcee9fea4fa85a42b4f1adc7dcb92a8d48ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/6706bcee9fea4fa85a42b4f1adc7dcb92a8d48ff"}],"sha":"e2236db818cd4a486afd956c62191787dfb312b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/e2236db818cd4a486afd956c62191787dfb312b1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/6706bcee9fea4fa85a42b4f1adc7dcb92a8d48ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T22:57:01Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T22:57:01Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"message":"fix(ui): gate device onboarding to admins\n\nThe API was always admin-only (test-connection/discover/create all\nrequire_admin), but the UI showed every user the ''+ Onboard a new device''\nbutton and an unguarded /onboard route — a requester could walk the whole\nwizard only to 403 at the first device call. OnboardPage now redirects\nnon-admins (same Navigate pattern as SettingsPage) and the EnvPicker\naffordance renders for admins only.\n\nAlso adds the password-UI capture script used for docs screenshots.","tree":{"sha":"93499b1d079af357f2982569b7a609fc464d6377","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/trees/93499b1d079af357f2982569b7a609fc464d6377"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/commits/6706bcee9fea4fa85a42b4f1adc7dcb92a8d48ff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/6706bcee9fea4fa85a42b4f1adc7dcb92a8d48ff","node_id":"C_kwDOSZdL19oAKDY3MDZiY2VlOWZlYTRmYTg1YTQyYjRmMWFkYzdkY2I5MmE4ZDQ4ZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/ef33b9c79d5ac43c37faab88af768e07cb258af8","sha":"ef33b9c79d5ac43c37faab88af768e07cb258af8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/ef33b9c79d5ac43c37faab88af768e07cb258af8"}],"sha":"6706bcee9fea4fa85a42b4f1adc7dcb92a8d48ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/6706bcee9fea4fa85a42b4f1adc7dcb92a8d48ff"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/ef33b9c79d5ac43c37faab88af768e07cb258af8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T22:08:29Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T22:08:29Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"message":"feat(auth): password change/reset with real session revocation; reject approved requests in UI\n\nPassword management (was: no way to change any password except editing the DB):\n- POST /api/users/me/password — self-service (any role): requires the CURRENT\n  password, bumps User.token_version, re-issues fresh cookies so the changing\n  session survives. Audited (user.password_changed, no secret material).\n- POST /api/users/{id}/password-reset — admin sets a NEW password (old ones are\n  one-way bcrypt hashes, never recoverable/viewable) and kicks every session of\n  the target. Audited with actor + target username.\n- Session revocation for stateless JWTs: tokens now carry a ''ver'' claim checked\n  against User.token_version on every request AND at refresh (a stale refresh\n  token can''t mint new sessions). Pre-claim tokens default ver=0 == the column\n  backfill, so live sessions survive the upgrade until the first change.\n  Migration d7e8f9a0b1c2 adds users.token_version.\n- UI: ''Change password'' in the user menu (all roles, modal with current/new/\n  confirm); Settings → Users section (admin): per-user reset with the explicit\n  note that passwords can only be replaced, never viewed.\n\nRequests: approved rows now offer ''Reject…'' alongside ''Apply now'' — the\nAPPROVED→REJECTED transition was always legal in the state machine and the API,\nbut the UI offered no exit except applying (painful for stale drift-blocked\nrequests). Characterization test pins the API behavior. No hard-delete by\ndesign: the change trail is compliance data (same reason device-delete is\nblocked while history exists); reject IS the kill switch.\n\nTests: +8 (password change/reset/revocation matrix, approved-reject). Backend\n494 passed; pyright 0 errors; ruff clean; frontend tsc/eslint/vitest clean.","tree":{"sha":"5bd4ee8146c33cd6553b6538b79a2ba873944ad6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/trees/5bd4ee8146c33cd6553b6538b79a2ba873944ad6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/commits/ef33b9c79d5ac43c37faab88af768e07cb258af8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/ef33b9c79d5ac43c37faab88af768e07cb258af8","node_id":"C_kwDOSZdL19oAKGVmMzNiOWM3OWQ1YWM0M2MzN2ZhYWI4OGFmNzY4ZTA3Y2IyNThhZjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/4eb9ffe5c589f29d04e0019d756c740fd00a622b","sha":"4eb9ffe5c589f29d04e0019d756c740fd00a622b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/4eb9ffe5c589f29d04e0019d756c740fd00a622b"}],"sha":"ef33b9c79d5ac43c37faab88af768e07cb258af8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/ef33b9c79d5ac43c37faab88af768e07cb258af8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/4eb9ffe5c589f29d04e0019d756c740fd00a622b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T21:21:24Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T21:21:24Z","email":"vishnu.v@karios.ai","name":"VishnuV"},"message":"fix: address full-project review — backend, frontend, security (35+ findings)\n\nBackend correctness:\n- pica8 _verify_applied matched only gigabit-ethernet elements → false\n  ''committed but not fully applied'' on every higher-speed port (te-/qe-);\n  now matches all _PORT_ELEMENTS + uses the hardened _safe_parse. aclose\n  documented (SSH is per-call; nothing to close — reviewer claim disproven).\n- ports.py _config_cache: unbounded dict → TTL+capacity-bound TTLCache;\n  invalidated on device offboard (new invalidate_device_caches).\n- Direct-write confirm-failure: backup + failure audit now committed through\n  the 502 rollback (was: device touched, zero trace).\n- resubmit clears reviewer_id (stale reviewer on re-queued requests).\n- Reconciler liveness N+1 → one GROUP BY; dead _latest_event_at removed.\n- Rate limiter: verified sub stashed in request.state (no double JWT decode;\n  cookie sessions now per-user keyed, not NAT-IP); _body canary tests.\n\nSecurity (review CRITICAL/HIGH):\n- CLI-injection guard: no-CR/LF pattern + length caps on ALL driver-bound\n  free text (PortChange/VlanChange/VrfChange/L3Change/OspfChange + port\n  schemas) — a newline in e.g. description was injectable into Jinja-rendered\n  CLI config. IP-format validators on ipv4/router_id/area.\n- SecurityHeadersMiddleware: X-Frame-Options/nosniff/Referrer-Policy/CSP,\n  HSTS when cookies are Secure, and same-origin enforcement on state-changing\n  requests (SameSite=Lax CSRF gap); NB_ALLOWED_ORIGINS escape hatch.\n- GET /api/audit admin-only (full log exposed per-user activity to requesters).\n- SSE: per-user concurrent stream cap (429) — fd/memory DoS bound.\n- allow_open_registration default ON → OFF (secure-by-default;\n  NB_ALLOW_OPEN_REGISTRATION=1 opts in). jwt_algorithm → HS256/384/512\n  allowlist; dead jwt_expiry_minutes removed.\n- SSH/NETCONF host-key verification knob (NB_SSH_STRICT_HOST_KEYS +\n  NB_SSH_KNOWN_HOSTS_PATH) wired into pica8; loud startup warning when off\n  outside development.\n- SPA: Bearer token no longer stored in JS-reachable state (Zustand) nor sent\n  as a header — cookie-only browser auth (XSS can''t exfiltrate the session).\n\nFrontend:\n- onError toasts on every approve/apply/reject/request-changes/resubmit\n  mutation (failures were silent); parseError now flattens object detail\n  ({code,message}) so 409 STATE_DRIFT reads properly.\n- DeviceSystemView 1,107 → 740 lines: VLAN/L3/OSPF/VRF forms extracted to\n  components/device-system/ (17 state atoms → 3 + per-form state).\n- DataTable: stable rowKeys prop (index keys broke reconciliation under live\n  filtering); ''''-vs-null cell semantics for action columns.\n- PortConfigEditor: reset on port.name change only (whole-object dep wiped\n  unsaved drafts on every 30s refetch/SSE event).\n- SearchResultsPage → TanStack Query (loading state, cache, no console.error).\n- OSPF query-key factory + invalidation after filing an OSPF request.\n- mapRequest runtime type guards (no bare as-casts on wire data).\n- isPlausibleIp tightened to real octet range; wizard reuses it.\n- Removed stale ''g l''/''g d'' env shortcuts; audit fetch gated to admins.\n\nGate: backend 486 passed (+30 new tests) / pyright 0 errors / ruff clean;\nfrontend tsc 0 / eslint 0 / vitest 62 passed.","tree":{"sha":"c173f65add798c6f35a5d99e2eb913d4c5dc80d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/trees/c173f65add798c6f35a5d99e2eb913d4c5dc80d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/git/commits/4eb9ffe5c589f29d04e0019d756c740fd00a622b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/4eb9ffe5c589f29d04e0019d756c740fd00a622b","node_id":"C_kwDOSZdL19oAKDRlYjlmZmU1YzU4OWYyOWQwNGUwMDE5ZDc1NmM3NDBmZDAwYTYyMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commit/9cbbb595216fa8d151818e78bfc14874d05d107a","sha":"9cbbb595216fa8d151818e78bfc14874d05d107a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/9cbbb595216fa8d151818e78bfc14874d05d107a"}],"sha":"4eb9ffe5c589f29d04e0019d756c740fd00a622b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/4eb9ffe5c589f29d04e0019d756c740fd00a622b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55404692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VishnuVuggepalli/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VishnuVuggepalli/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VishnuVuggepalli/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VishnuVuggepalli/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/VishnuVuggepalli","id":55404692,"login":"VishnuVuggepalli","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1NDA0Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VishnuVuggepalli/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VishnuVuggepalli/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VishnuVuggepalli/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VishnuVuggepalli/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/VishnuVuggepalli/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VishnuVuggepalli","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VishnuVuggepalli/Northbound/commits/9cbbb595216fa8d151818e78bfc14874d05d107a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T18:43:12Z","email":"55404692+VishnuVuggepa