_url":"https://github.com/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commit/2ddae3c9b7055058a73c50e17d57df390aa8dd41","sha":"2ddae3c9b7055058a73c50e17d57df390aa8dd41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commits/2ddae3c9b7055058a73c50e17d57df390aa8dd41"}],"sha":"1e28cc25ae408293d77fbc635c21770bdb28866f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commits/1e28cc25ae408293d77fbc635c21770bdb28866f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171240994?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/xalatechnologies","id":171240994,"login":"xalatechnologies","node_id":"U_kgDOCjTuIg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commits/2ddae3c9b7055058a73c50e17d57df390aa8dd41/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T18:34:09Z","email":"info@xala.no","name":"xalatechnologies"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T18:34:09Z","email":"info@xala.no","name":"xalatechnologies"},"message":"feat(phase-19b): close deferred items · email channel · quiet hours · AI ranking · authenticity score · event postpone\n\nCloses the de-deferable items from the prior phase (Resend key now\navailable) and a couple of architectural cleanups:\n\n- email: convex/email.ts Resend wrapper (V8 fetch). Email channel added\n  as 4th leg of notify.dispatch — opt-in via notifyPrefs.email; lifecycle\n  kinds (welcome / subscription_*) bypass the toggle and always send.\n- emailVerification: token-hash-based verify flow.\n  internal.emailVerification._initiate generates a 32-byte token,\n  stores its sha-256 (never the plaintext), emails the user a 24h link.\n  auth.confirm validates + stamps emailVerificationTime. Password\n  signups schedule it from the auth callback; Discord OAuth signups\n  skip (Discord vouches for the email). Quiet no-op when RESEND_API_KEY\n  is unset.\n- notify: NEW _dispatchAfterQuietHours internal action + quiet-hours\n  fields on notifyPrefs (start, end, timezone). Push + telegram defer\n  to next allowed window via scheduler.runAfter; in-app + email always\n  fire; lifecycle kinds bypass; cross-midnight windows handled.\n- feed.personalized: new opt-in rankByAi arg. Pure-function blend:\n  0.40 × aiConfidence + 0.25 × trustScore + 0.20 × recency-decay\n  (24h half-life, 7d floor) + 0.15 × pick-confidence enum. Default\n  false to preserve chronological order on legacy callers.\n- applications: scoreApplicationAuthenticity action runs Anthropic Haiku\n  on every submitted application; advisory aiAuthenticityScore +\n  aiAuthenticityReasoning surface to admins in the review queue.\n  Output is advisory only — never auto-suspends, never auto-rejects.\n- events.postpone: admin mutation that flips an upcoming/live event\n  back to upcoming with a new startsAt, MFA-gated, audit-logged.\n  Rejects on completed / cancelled / past timestamps.\n- discordInbound retirement: legacy convex/discordInbound.ts deleted +\n  Settings.tsx legacy card removed. The comprehensive convex/discord/*\n  module is the single Discord surface now (see /dashboard/settings/discord\n  for the full UI).\n- BPMN-001/004/006/015/016 updated to remove DEFERRED labels and\n  describe the new behavior.\n\nSchema additions:\n- users.{emailVerificationTokenHash, emailVerificationSentAt,\n  emailVerificationExpiresAt} + by_emailVerificationTokenHash index\n- notifyPrefs.{email, quietHoursStart, quietHoursEnd, quietHoursTimezone}\n- applications.{aiAuthenticityScore, aiAuthenticityReasoning, aiAuthenticityScoredAt}\n\nVerified: pnpm typecheck (8 packages) clean · pnpm test 86/86 ·\n4 thin-app strict-mode greps 0 violations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1331cdf3213a20d80be3079567cfc0f92a0d9fc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/git/trees/1331cdf3213a20d80be3079567cfc0f92a0d9fc2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/git/commits/2ddae3c9b7055058a73c50e17d57df390aa8dd41","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171240994?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/xalatechnologies","id":171240994,"login":"xalatechnologies","node_id":"U_kgDOCjTuIg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commit/2ddae3c9b7055058a73c50e17d57df390aa8dd41","node_id":"C_kwDOSZqOSNoAKDJkZGFlM2M5YjcwNTUwNThhNzNjNTBlMTdkNTdkZjM5MGFhOGRkNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commit/125d9e0ef602c017e8ffade458e4698ebc56f843","sha":"125d9e0ef602c017e8ffade458e4698ebc56f843","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commits/125d9e0ef602c017e8ffade458e4698ebc56f843"}],"sha":"2ddae3c9b7055058a73c50e17d57df390aa8dd41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commits/2ddae3c9b7055058a73c50e17d57df390aa8dd41"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171240994?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/xalatechnologies","id":171240994,"login":"xalatechnologies","node_id":"U_kgDOCjTuIg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commits/125d9e0ef602c017e8ffade458e4698ebc56f843/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T18:23:43Z","email":"info@xala.no","name":"xalatechnologies"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T18:23:43Z","email":"info@xala.no","name":"xalatechnologies"},"message":"feat(phase-19): drift sweep · stripe idempotency · grace period · lifecycle notify · BPMN alignment\n\nCloses the gap between BPMN-001/002/003/008/010/011/012/013/014/015 and\nthe code, plus a handful of audit findings from the M20/M24 sweep:\n\n- auth: write user.signup audit + schedule onUserSignup welcome dispatch\n- notify: lifecycle kinds (welcome, subscription_*) bypass per-kind toggles;\n  NOTIFY_DEDUP_WINDOW_MS overridable\n- stripe: new stripeEvents table + stripeIdempotency.claim mutation;\n  webhook short-circuits on Stripe re-deliveries\n- subscriptions: gracePeriodEndsAt + isAccessActive helper; lifecycle\n  notifies on transitions; GRACE_PERIOD_DAYS overridable (default 3d)\n- events.reviewEvent: gateOnMfaIfEnrolled (BPMN-010 §preconditions)\n- disputes.transition: optional overrideGrade flips pick.grade and writes\n  paired pick.grade.overridden audit row (BPMN-011, NFR-006)\n- streams: _archiveStreamRoom flips channel inactive on live→offline edge\n- picks/ai: gradingExplanation action + picks.gradeExplanation field;\n  suggestPick degrades gracefully on missing key\n- channels.list: surfaces both public and subscriber-tier channels with\n  requiredAccess for the UI lock\n- earnings: earningsHistory query + shared platformFees.ts (PLATFORM_FEE_RATE_BPS\n  overridable)\n- shared/sportKeyMap: tennis + rugby coverage expanded\n- BPMN: all 16 files reconciled to current code; module-mapping links\n  repointed to authoritative docs/modules slugs; entitlements references\n  removed in favor of subscription.status + isAccessActive; deferred items\n  (email verify, AI ranking, Stripe refund, quiet hours, persona-mismatch,\n  postponement / forfeit) explicitly marked DEFERRED\n\nVerified: pnpm typecheck (8 packages) clean · pnpm test 86/86 · build clean ·\n4 thin-app strict-mode greps 0 violations · 0 stale module slugs ·\n0 entitlements references in BPMN.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{