/commits/53b12525985c98839a056fb7fb2e567de06ccb32/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T16:02:22Z","email":"info@xala.no","name":"xalatechnologies"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T16:02:22Z","email":"info@xala.no","name":"xalatechnologies"},"message":"feat(phase-18): wire creator-side Copilot · auto-grader observability · finalize Discord scaffolding\n\nUI\n- Lazy-route /admin/disputes and /admin/coupons in App.tsx\n- New account routes: /messages, /watchlists, /copilot\n- New creator-studio routes: /copilot, /settings/discord, /discord/discussions\n- Creator-persona Copilot page (filters conversations to persona=''creator'')\n- Auto-grader observability section on /admin: per-grade counts and a\n  sample table of recent auto-graded picks for fast misgrade spot-checks\n\nConvex\n- admin.autoGraderStats query rolls up pick.graded.* audit entries with\n  metadata.autoGraded=true into win/loss/push/void counts\n- Split convex/discord/inbound.ts internalMutation into a separate non-Node\n  module so the action file can stay ''use node''\n- Narrow hexToUint8Array return to Uint8Array<ArrayBuffer> so WebCrypto\n  BufferSource constraint holds under tightened TS lib types\n- Carryover from earlier session: aiCopilot/, discord/ (channels, delivery,\n  events, gdpr, inbound, integrations, oauth, retry, sentiment, threads),\n  shared/sportKeyMap, schema additions\n\nDS\n- Discord domain components (IntegrationCard, channel mapper, alert rule\n  editor, sync-direction selector, connect button, thread-link badge,\n  delivery log table, discussion summary), CopilotResponsibleNote,\n  CopilotChat streaming + citations\n\nVerification\n- pnpm typecheck → all packages Done\n- pnpm test → 86/86 pass\n- pnpm --filter @digipicks/web build → ✓ built in 1.26s\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b2741b454bad96e22e2080ebaa05323125dbafc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/git/trees/b2741b454bad96e22e2080ebaa05323125dbafc5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/git/commits/53b12525985c98839a056fb7fb2e567de06ccb32","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171240994?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/xalatechnologies","id":171240994,"login":"xalatechnologies","node_id":"U_kgDOCjTuIg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commit/53b12525985c98839a056fb7fb2e567de06ccb32","node_id":"C_kwDOSZqOSNoAKDUzYjEyNTI1OTg1Yzk4ODM5YTA1NmZiN2ZiMmU1NjdkZTA2Y2NiMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commit/925adde8c964c6e3c76818a0eed785e13baf27fd","sha":"925adde8c964c6e3c76818a0eed785e13baf27fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commits/925adde8c964c6e3c76818a0eed785e13baf27fd"}],"sha":"53b12525985c98839a056fb7fb2e567de06ccb32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commits/53b12525985c98839a056fb7fb2e567de06ccb32"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171240994?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/xalatechnologies","id":171240994,"login":"xalatechnologies","node_id":"U_kgDOCjTuIg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commits/925adde8c964c6e3c76818a0eed785e13baf27fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:40:42Z","email":"info@xala.no","name":"xalatechnologies"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:40:42Z","email":"info@xala.no","name":"xalatechnologies"},"message":"feat(phase-17): wire Phase 16 backend into UI — coupons admin · audit metrics · trial days · Discord integrations · Copilot chat\n\nThe \"make every Phase 16 surface usable\" pass. Five wirings, one DS component\n(CopilotChat), one new admin page (Coupons), one new account page (Copilot).\nAll five carry-forward UIs from the Phase 16 commit are now live.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n17a — Coupon admin page\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n- apps/web/src/pages/admin/Coupons.tsx — table of active coupons + new\n  coupon form. Wired to api.coupons.{list, create, archive}. Shows\n  redemption count vs cap, expiry, and the underlying Stripe coupon ID.\n  Admin enters the Stripe coupon ID by hand (Stripe is the source of\n  truth; this surface manages issuance + caps).\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n17b — Audit metrics card\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n- pages/admin/Admin.tsx adds a Retention section: 6 metric tiles for\n  audit-log entries by age (7d / 30d / 90d / 1y / 1y+ / 2y+) plus the\n  configured AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS. Sourced from api.audit.metrics. No\n  deletion happens — append-only contract preserved; this drives the\n  admin''s policy decisions.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n17c — Trial days on Products\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n- dashboard/Products.tsx new-tier prompt asks for optional trial period.\n  Trial days surface as a feature pill on the tier card.\n- pricingTiers.create + pricingTiers.update extended with optional\n  trialDays arg.\n- stripe.createCheckoutSession picks up trialDays via tierId arg →\n  passes subscription_data[trial_period_days] (already wired Phase 16d).\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n17d — Discord integrations card\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n- dashboard/Settings.tsx new DiscordIntegrationsCard component (defined\n  inline with the page since it only renders here). Lists existing\n  integrations from api.discordInbound.listForCreator with pause toggle.\n  Manual connect form (guildId + guildName) until OAuth ships in a\n  follow-up.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n17e — AI Copilot chat surface\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n- packages/ds/src/components/domain/CopilotChat/* (NEW) — multi-turn\n  copilot surface. User / assistant / tool roles render with distinct\n  bubble + alignment. Citations render as pill-buttons under each\n  assistant turn. Optional \"Show tool trace\" toggle reveals the\n  intermediate tool turns for debugging.\n- apps/web/src/account/pages/Copilot.tsx (NEW) — subscriber-side\n  copilot. Two-column: conversations list + active chat. Wired to\n  api.copilot.{startConversation, appendUserMessage, respond,\n  myConversations, messages, archiveConversation}.\n- Persona forced to ''customer'' for now; creator-side copilot ships when\n  /dashboard/copilot lands.\n\nVerification:\n- pnpm typecheck (8/8 strict)\n- pnpm test (81 tests still passing — no backend regression)\n- pnpm build (470 kB → 150 kB gz, +1.5kB for CopilotChat)\n- npx convex dev --once → 4.08s push (pricingTiers.create + .update\n  schemas updated for trialDays arg)\n\nCarry-forward (small):\n- AdminRoutes wire-up for /admin/coupons (Coupons page is built; routing\n  is one line in the user''s AdminRoutes file).\n- AccountRoutes wire-up for /account/copilot (same — one line in the\n  user''s existing AccountRoutes).\n- Discord OAuth flow + bot ingestion for the actual inbound message\n  pipeline (the schema + admin/creator surfaces are functional today).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3d0a7be95ffb36cc606c6d9d1dfd0d6fb9cf69e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/git/trees/3d0a7be95ffb36cc606c6d9d1dfd0d6fb9cf69e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/git/commits/925adde8c964c6e3c76818a0eed785e13baf27fd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171240994?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/xalatechnologies","id":171240994,"login":"xalatechnologies","node_id":"U_kgDOCjTuIg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commit/925adde8c964c6e3c76818a0eed785e13baf27fd","node_id":"C_kwDOSZqOSNoAKDkyNWFkZGU4Yzk2NGM2ZTNjNzY4MThhMGVlZDc4NWUxM2JhZjI3ZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commit/6fe807f0a8672c7f20f7d4544fc247b4df1801e7","sha":"6fe807f0a8672c7f20f7d4544fc247b4df1801e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commits/6fe807f0a8672c7f20f7d4544fc247b4df1801e7"}],"sha":"925adde8c964c6e3c76818a0eed785e13baf27fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commits/925adde8c964c6e3c76818a0eed785e13baf27fd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171240994?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/xalatechnologies","id":171240994,"login":"xalatechnologies","node_id":"U_kgDOCjTuIg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/commits/6fe807f0a8672c7f20f7d4544fc247b4df1801e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:31:13Z","email":"info@xala.no","name":"xalatechnologies"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:31:13Z","email":"info@xala.no","name":"xalatechnologies"},"message":"feat(phase-16): auto-grader · premium-event gate · coupons + trials · Discord inbound · AI Copilot v1\n\nThe \"make every module ship-complete\" pass. Six items in one chain — all\nbackend; UI surfaces wired in a follow-up. 81 tests / typecheck strict /\nbuild clean / npx convex dev pushed in 3.91s.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n16a — Pick auto-grader (M09)\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n- convex/autoGrader.ts: 15-min cron iterates `events.status=''completed''`\n  with scores set, finds pending picks via new `picks.by_event_and_status`\n  index, parses h2h / spread / total markets, grades atomically.\n- Aggressive parsing per the user''s explicit policy decision: grade\n  every pick we can recognize. Unparseable markets stay pending for\n  manual admin grading.\n- Helpers (pure functions, exposed via _testHooks for unit tests):\n  - americanToDecimal · parseUnits · parseLine\n  - detectSide (mascot-aware: \"Chiefs\" matches \"Kansas City Chiefs\",\n    bails when both teams share the mascot)\n  - detectOverUnder · classifyMarket · gradePick\n- Net-units format: \"+0.91u\" / \"-1u\" / \"0u\" — derived from American odds.\n- 9 unit tests covering parsers + h2h/spread/total/push paths.\n- Audit-logged via existing pick.graded.{win|loss|push} action with\n  metadata.autoGraded=true.\n- Fan-out via `notify.onPickGraded` so subscribers + savers get the\n  in-app + push + Telegram alert.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n16b — Premium-event server enforcement (M23)\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n- picks.create rejects (premium | vip) + eventId where the event''s\n  verificationStatus !== ''admin_verified''. Closes the abuse vector:\n  creators monetizing self-submitted unverified events. Free picks\n  unaffected so creators can seed events while review is pending.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n16c — Audit retention metrics (M25)\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n- audit.metrics admin query: row counts bucketed by age (7d / 30d /\n  90d / 1y / 1y+ / 2y+) + AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS env (default 730).\n- No deletion — audit logs stay append-only by platform contract.\n  Admin uses the buckets to drive policy decisions.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n16d — Stripe coupons + trial days (M19)\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n- pricingTiers.trialDays optional field.\n- couponCodes table (code, stripeCouponId, percentOff,\n  amountOffCents, maxRedemptions, redemptionCount, expiresAt,\n  archived). Indexed by_code + by_archived.\n- coupons.{list, lookup, create, archive, _incrementRedemption}.\n  Admin-only create + archive, audit-logged.\n- stripe.createCheckoutSession accepts couponCode + tierId args:\n  - couponCode → resolves through coupons._lookupCoupon, attaches\n    discounts[0][coupon] + metadata.couponCode.\n  - tierId → resolves trialDays, sets subscription_data[trial_period_days].\n- Stripe webhook (invoice.paid) increments couponCodes.redemptionCount\n  via internal.coupons._incrementRedemption so admin caps fire.\n- Stripe is the source of truth for the actual discount; this is the\n  platform mirror for issuance + caps + audit.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n16e — Discord inbound (schema + scaffolding) (M20)\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n- 5 new tables — discordIntegrations, discordChannelSyncs,\n  discordMessageImports, discordSentimentSummaries, discordDeliveryLogs.\n- discordInbound.ts: connectGuild (idempotent), configureChannelSync\n  (creator/admin), pauseIntegration, revokeIntegration (admin),\n  listForCreator, channelSyncs.\n- Action stubs importChannelMessages + generateDiscussionSummary\n  return { skipped: true } without DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN — the schema +\n  surfaces are functional today; Bot API ingestion lands in a\n  follow-up.\n- All transitions audit-logged.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n16f — AI Copilot v1 (M24)\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n- 2 new tables — aiConversations (userId, persona, title,\n  messageCount, archivedAt), aiMessages (role, body, model, citations,\n  inputTokens/outputTokens). Indexed for the chat list + history scroll.\n- copilot.ts ships:\n  - Public mutations: startConversation, appendUserMessage,\n    archiveConversation\n  - Public queries: myConversations, messages\n  - Public action: respond (rate-limited via stripeCheckout bucket)\n- Tool-use loop runs up to 3 iterations against Anthropic Claude Hauku\n  with two tools:\n    lookupCreator(handle)        → creators.by_handle\n    creatorPerformance(creatorId) → picks.by_creator + win-rate aggregate\n- System prompts split by persona — customer / creator. Both demand\n  citations + sample-size context + \"no gambling advice\".\n- Citations harvested from tool results into aiMessages.citations.\n- Tool turns persisted as role=''tool'' rows so the UI can render the\n  trace; user/assistant turns are the chat surface.\n- Quiet no-op when ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is unset.\n\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nVerification\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n- pnpm typecheck (8/8 strict)\n- pnpm test (81 tests, +12 from auto-grader unit tests + lifecycle audit\n  test)\n- pnpm build (470 kB → 150 kB gz)\n- npx convex dev --once → 3.91s push\n- 12 crons total (auto-grade-picks joins the schedule)\n\nNotes for deploy:\n- New env: AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS (display only, default 730);\n  DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN (gates inbound import action — not yet\n  implemented).\n- New cron: auto-grade-picks (15min). Runs aggressively — admins\n  should monitor early days for misgrades. The grade-immutability lock\n  (NFR-006) still stands; admins resolve disputes via M17 instead of\n  re-grading.\n\nUI carry-forward:\n- Discord inbound creator-side card + admin queue.\n- Copilot chat surface — DS CopilotChat + apps/web/src/account/Copilot\n  page. Backend is ready to drive it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"390f54120fb40da9b403fc6a0692508d5048a39d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/git/trees/390f54120fb40da9b403fc6a0692508d5048a39d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xalatechnologies/DigiPicks-v2/git/commits/6fe807f0a8672c7f20f7d4544fc247b4df1801e7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171240994?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xalatechnologies/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https:/