lowing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/indraakkk/ActiveStats/commit/f330b8b2537f9cf0e0893b4b94e37768af8350aa","node_id":"C_kwDOSZ5x8doAKGYzMzBiOGIyNTM3ZjljZjBlMDg5M2I0Yjk0ZTM3NzY4YWY4MzUwYWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/indraakkk/ActiveStats/commit/f31534c37128d7daa48b5c5fd198ad29580ceb38","sha":"f31534c37128d7daa48b5c5fd198ad29580ceb38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/indraakkk/ActiveStats/commits/f31534c37128d7daa48b5c5fd198ad29580ceb38"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/indraakkk/ActiveStats/commit/c87f9b9dfa01265aa70aaf878b3b1eb69f114ce2","sha":"c87f9b9dfa01265aa70aaf878b3b1eb69f114ce2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/indraakkk/ActiveStats/commits/c87f9b9dfa01265aa70aaf878b3b1eb69f114ce2"}],"sha":"f330b8b2537f9cf0e0893b4b94e37768af8350aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/indraakkk/ActiveStats/commits/f330b8b2537f9cf0e0893b4b94e37768af8350aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/indraakkk/ActiveStats/commits/c87f9b9dfa01265aa70aaf878b3b1eb69f114ce2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T04:30:45Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T04:30:45Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 3 - Konva editor with lossless PNG export\n\nStandalone editor app at apps/overlay-editor (port 3001). Drop a photo,\nadd text/stat-card/route/divider overlays, drag/resize/rotate, then\nexport PNG at the photo''s native resolution.\n\nArchitecture:\n- Overlay positions stored as relative coords [0..1] in packages/shared\n  types (OverlayElement union). Same set scales to live preview and\n  export without recomputation - anti-pattern dodged from spec.\n- src/lib/export.ts is the engineering heart. Renders to a fresh\n  OFFSCREEN Konva stage at native imageWidth x imageHeight with\n  pixelRatio: 1 so overlays stay sharp (not upscaled from preview).\n- Effect boundaries per s1.5.5: loadImage uses Effect.async with\n  on-interrupt cleanup so unmount mid-export aborts the load and\n  dereferences the partial Image. Konva calls inside renderToBlob are\n  imperative and wrapped once in Effect.try at the boundary - not\n  every Konva.add() wrapped in Effect.sync.\n- State in Atoms (s1.5.4): imageAtom, overlaysAtom, selectedIdAtom,\n  canvasDisplayAtom, selectedOverlayAtom (derived). No useState for\n  cross-component state.\n- Live canvas uses react-konva with a Transformer attached to the\n  selected node. Drag/transform end handlers convert absolute pixels\n  back to relative coords before writing the store.\n- Export action is a runtimeAtom.fn(Effect.fnUntraced(...)) so it\n  inherits Effect cancellation on unmount.\n\nVerification protocol per s1.5.0:\n- Verified Effect.async cleanup signature against\n  github.com/Effect-TS/effect source - register callback can return\n  void or Effect<void, never, R>, the cleanup Effect runs on fiber\n  interruption. Spec snippet matched the source.\n- Pinned react-konva@^18 (not the latest @19 which needs React 19) to\n  preserve React 18 per spec.\n- Pinned @effect/platform@^0.94.5 + effect@^3.18 to satisfy\n  @effect-atom/atom-react@0.5.0''s peer dep range.\n\nAcceptance verified locally:\n- pnpm typecheck across all 4 workspace projects: green\n- pnpm build across all 4 workspace projects: green\n  (overlay-editor bundle 678 KiB / 213 KiB gzip - Konva is the bulk)\n- All 13 editor modules transpile via Vite dev server (HTTP 200)\n- No Vite/esbuild errors\n\nManual browser verification of the lossless claim (the spec''s key\ntest) still needed: upload a photo of known dimensions (e.g.\n4032x3024), add overlays, export, confirm output PNG is exactly\n4032x3024 with sharp overlay edges.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_011aLjt13XLa9iRVaDSLpV1w","tree":{"sha":"a66e5408a641118060c5e1b4ac5cd7750e1038c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/indraakkk/ActiveStats/git/trees/a66e5408a641118060c5e1b4ac5cd7750e1038c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/indraakkk/ActiveStats/git/commits/c87f9b9dfa01265aa70aaf878b3b1eb69f114ce2","verification":{"payload":"tree a66e5408a641118060c5e1b4ac5cd7750e1038c5\nparent f31534c37128d7daa48b5c5fd198ad29580ceb38\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1778473845 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1778473845 +0000\n\nPhase 3 - Konva editor with lossless PNG export\n\nStandalone editor app at apps/overlay-editor (port 3001). Drop a photo,\nadd text/stat-card/route/divider overlays, drag/resize/rotate, then\nexport PNG at the photo''s native resolution.\n\nArchitecture:\n- Overlay positions stored as relative coords [0..1] in packages/shared\n  types (OverlayElement union). Same set scales to live preview and\n  export without recomputation - anti-pattern dodged from spec.\n- src/lib/export.ts is the engineering heart. Renders to a fresh\n  OFFSCREEN Konva stage at native imageWidth x imageHeight with\n  pixelRatio: 1 so overlays stay sharp (not upscaled from preview).\n- Effect boundaries per s1.5.5: loadImage uses Effect.async with\n  on-interrupt cleanup so unmount mid-export aborts the load and\n  dereferences the partial Image. Konva calls inside renderToBlob are\n  imperative and wrapped once in Effect.try at the boundary - not\n  every Konva.add() wrapped in Effect.sync.\n- State in Atoms (s1.5.4): imageAtom, overlaysAtom, selectedIdAtom,\n  canvasDisplayAtom, selectedOverlayAtom (derived). No useState for\n  cross-component state.\n- Live canvas uses react-konva with a Transformer attached to the\n  selected node. Drag/transform end handlers convert absolute pixels\n  back to relative coords before writing the store.\n- Export action is a runtimeAtom.fn(Effect.fnUntraced(...)) so it\n  inherits Effect cancellation on unmount.\n\nVerification protocol per s1.5.0:\n- Verified Effect.async cleanup signature against\n  github.com/Effect-TS/effect source - register callback can return\n  void or Effect<void, never, R>, the cleanup Effect runs on fiber\n  interruption. Spec snippet matched the source.\n- Pinned react-konva@^18 (not the latest @19 which needs React 19) to\n  preserve React 18 per spec.\n- Pinned @effect/platform@^0.94.5 + effect@^3.18 to satisfy\n  @effect-atom/atom-react@0.5.0''s peer dep range.\n\nAcceptance verified locally:\n- pnpm typecheck across all 4 workspace projects: green\n- pnpm build across all 4 workspace projects: green\n  (overlay-editor bundle 678 KiB / 213 KiB gzip - Konva is the bulk)\n- All 13 editor modules transpile via Vite dev server (HTTP 200)\n- No Vite/esbuild errors\n\nManual browser verification of the lossless claim (the spec''s key\ntest) still needed: upload a photo of known dimensions (e.g.\n4032x3024), add overlays, export, confirm output PNG is exactly\n4032x3024 with sharp overlay edges.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_011aLjt13XLa9iRVaDSLpV1w\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHUlXmkf\nPsaE1ObLHXG3QXey0TKFZpv2Fei7XvzTwj85EpnhWbiSdutkHxG+RH7At+qicbP7lHhBWZhUhiTZ\ncA0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-11T04:30:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/indraakkk/ActiveStats/commit/c87f9b9dfa01265aa70aaf878b3b1eb69f114ce2","node_id":"C_kwDOSZ5x8doAKGM4N2Y5YjlkZmEwMTI2NWFhNzBhYWY4NzhiM2IxZWI2OWYxMTRjZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/indraakkk/ActiveStats/commit/f31534c37128d7daa48b5c5fd198ad29580ceb38","sha":"f31534c37128d7daa48b5c5fd198ad29580ceb38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/indraakkk/ActiveStats/commits/f31534c37128d7daa48b5c5fd198ad29580ceb38"}],"sha":"c87f9b9dfa01265aa70aaf878b3b1eb69f114ce2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/indraakkk/ActiveStats/commits/c87f9b9dfa01265aa70aaf878b3b1eb69f114ce2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/indraakkk/ActiveStats/commits/f31534c37128d7daa48b5c5fd198ad29580ceb38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T04:17:04Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T04:17:04Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 2 - Cloudflare Worker for Strava OAuth token exchange\n\nauth-worker/ lives in the monorepo but outside the pnpm workspace\n(different runtime, different bundler) - shares types via tsconfig\npath alias. Worker exchanges Strava `code` for tokens (and refreshes\nexisting tokens) so the `client_secret` never reaches the browser.\n\nImplementation in Effect-TS per SPEC s1.5: tagged errors, Effect.gen\ncontrol flow, Schema validation of both the inbound request body AND\nStrava''s response (defense in depth). Added Athlete + OAuthTokenResponse\nschemas in packages/shared so the worker and the eventual shell app\nvalidate against the same shape.\n\nThe spec''s catch chain only handles BadRequest, StravaUpstreamError,\nand defects. Added an Effect.catchAll to cover HttpClient transport\nfailures that would otherwise bubble out as a generic 500 - now they\nreturn a structured 502. Also added Effect.scoped before Effect.provide\nto discharge the Scope requirement that http.execute introduces.\n\nTooling:\n- CI now installs+typechecks auth-worker (it''s outside pnpm so the\n  root pnpm typecheck doesn''t reach it).\n- deploy-worker.yml uses cloudflare/wrangler-action with path-filtered\n  trigger (auth-worker/** or packages/shared/src/types/strava.ts).\n- Manual deploy path documented in README (wrangler login -> secret\n  put -> deploy) plus curl smoke-tests.\n\nWrangler dry-run bundle: 1868 KiB / 364 KiB gzip - well under the\n1 MiB CF Workers limit.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_011aLjt13XLa9iRVaDSLpV1w","tree":{"sha":"d30afcc726e5ea0f766ff8ab14ce7e3072451afa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/indraakkk/ActiveStats/git/trees/d30afcc726e5ea0f766ff8ab14ce7e3072451afa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/indraakkk/ActiveStats/git/commits/f31534c37128d7daa48b5c5fd198ad29580ceb38","verification":{"payload":"tree d30afcc726e5ea0f766ff8ab14ce7e3072451afa\nparent 9d37a82155d509a0c20d4f73fa586517651afc55\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1778473024 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1778473024 +0000\n\nPhase 2 - Cloudflare Worker for Strava OAuth token exchange\n\nauth-worker/ lives in the monorepo but outside the pnpm workspace\n(different runtime, different bundler) - shares types via tsconfig\npath alias. Worker exchanges Strava `code` for tokens (and refreshes\nexisting tokens) so the `client_secret` never reaches the browser.\n\nImplementation in Effect-TS per SPEC s1.5: tagged errors, Effect.gen\ncontrol flow, Schema validation of both the inbound request body AND\nStrava''s response (defense in depth). Added Athlete + OAuthTokenResponse\nschemas in packages/shared so the worker and the eventual shell app\nvalidate against the same shape.\n\nThe spec''s catch chain only handles BadRequest, StravaUpstreamError,\nand defects. Added an Effect.catchAll to cover HttpClient transport\nfailures that would otherwise bubble out as a generic 500 - now they\nreturn a structured 502. Also added Effect.scoped before Effect.provide\nto discharge the Scope requirement that http.execute introduces.\n\nTooling:\n- CI now installs+typechecks auth-worker (it''s outside pnpm so the\n  root pnpm typecheck doesn''t reach it).\n- deploy-worker.yml uses cloudflare/wrangler-action with path-filtered\n  trigger (auth-worker/** or packages/shared/src/types/strava.ts).\n- Manual deploy path documented in README (wrangler login -> secret\n  put -> deploy) plus curl smoke-tests.\n\nWrangler dry-run bundle: 1868 KiB / 364 KiB gzip - well under the\n1 MiB CF Workers limit.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_011aLjt13XLa9iRVaDSLpV1w\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLSHdywb\nQFtQkeOdGHQF4nd6/oD4THYiKtaW6Dq8Z+aC/FhCnbTfA4XwfNq64cuFOmYdbz2YB2wLFu0i/7dF\npA8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-11T04:17:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81