ions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commit/48cdbbe7afafec08cec05ea4ac0c954b251aeb9e","node_id":"C_kwDOSaMNktoAKDQ4Y2RiYmU3YWZhZmVjMDhjZWMwNWVhNGFjMGM5NTRiMjUxYWViOWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commit/b20ccb68c12632a40455d852926b710f4b857eab","sha":"b20ccb68c12632a40455d852926b710f4b857eab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/b20ccb68c12632a40455d852926b710f4b857eab"}],"sha":"48cdbbe7afafec08cec05ea4ac0c954b251aeb9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/48cdbbe7afafec08cec05ea4ac0c954b251aeb9e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6631578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shpilevoy","id":6631578,"login":"shpilevoy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzE1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/b20ccb68c12632a40455d852926b710f4b857eab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T16:55:29Z","email":"nick@shpil.io","name":"Nikita Shpilevoy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T16:55:29Z","email":"nick@shpil.io","name":"Nikita Shpilevoy"},"message":"fix(healthex): stop firing reconcile on every page refresh\n\nTwo on-mount fan-outs (HealthExConnections + ConnectHealthEx polling)\nwere unconditional — each refresh spawned N Airflow DAG runs per row.\nTwo guards:\n\n1. Only reconcile PENDING_CONSENT rows on mount. Rows that already\n   resolved a healthex_patient_id don''t gain anything from on-demand\n   reconcile — the periodic 30-min DAG tick catches revocations with\n   acceptable freshness. Most refreshes now fire ZERO reconciles.\n2. Per-project sessionStorage debounce (30s). Rapid refresh (dev,\n   back-forward, opening the page multiple times) coalesces into one\n   DAG run. Storage key is ''healthex.reconcile.lastFired.<project_id>''.\n\nFor a user with one resolved row, page refresh fires zero DAG runs\n(down from one). For a user mid-onboarding (one PENDING row), first\nrefresh fires one, next 5 within 30s fire zero.\n\nSame debounce applied in ConnectHealthEx so the polling-loop kickoff\ndoesn''t rethrow the reconcile on rapid remounts.","tree":{"sha":"1917dcc8aa51b3823074dbb0841d39abc33739b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/git/trees/1917dcc8aa51b3823074dbb0841d39abc33739b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/git/commits/b20ccb68c12632a40455d852926b710f4b857eab","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6631578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shpilevoy","id":6631578,"login":"shpilevoy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzE1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commit/b20ccb68c12632a40455d852926b710f4b857eab","node_id":"C_kwDOSaMNktoAKGIyMGNjYjY4YzEyNjMyYTQwNDU1ZDg1MjkyNmI3MTBmNGI4NTdlYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commit/8c3de69ced5049a2d02cdf6520b8e08ec9f1035f","sha":"8c3de69ced5049a2d02cdf6520b8e08ec9f1035f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/8c3de69ced5049a2d02cdf6520b8e08ec9f1035f"}],"sha":"b20ccb68c12632a40455d852926b710f4b857eab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/b20ccb68c12632a40455d852926b710f4b857eab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6631578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shpilevoy","id":6631578,"login":"shpilevoy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzE1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/8c3de69ced5049a2d02cdf6520b8e08ec9f1035f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T16:18:49Z","email":"nick@shpil.io","name":"Nikita Shpilevoy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T16:18:49Z","email":"nick@shpil.io","name":"Nikita Shpilevoy"},"message":"refactor(healthex): robust redirectUri append + drop stale CLEAR-only warning\n\nTwo changes prompted by Diego''s confirmation that the admin-side\nRedirect URLs config was solved with HealthEx in the 2026-07-01 meeting:\n\n- Swap the ''&redirectUri=<encoded>'' string concat for URL.searchParams.set.\n  The concat assumed the onboarding URL always carries a ''?xid=...''; if\n  HealthEx ever ships a version without the xid, the concat produces\n  ''link&redirectUri=X'' which is malformed. searchParams.set handles both\n  cases and matches the pattern healthtree-platform already uses on the\n  SvelteKit side.\n- Drop the CLEAR-only warning from HealthExConnectionsProps.redirectUri —\n  no longer applicable now that the admin config is correct.","tree":{"sha":"c020d83b6268a54e38f9961670c28a1e048b6088","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/git/trees/c020d83b6268a54e38f9961670c28a1e048b6088"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/git/commits/8c3de69ced5049a2d02cdf6520b8e08ec9f1035f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6631578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shpilevoy","id":6631578,"login":"shpilevoy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzE1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commit/8c3de69ced5049a2d02cdf6520b8e08ec9f1035f","node_id":"C_kwDOSaMNktoAKDhjM2RlNjljZWQ1MDQ5YTJkMDJjZGY2NTIwYjhlMDhlYzlmMTAzNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commit/7150b8a371ee69347fc89c23eb969cf97d24350b","sha":"7150b8a371ee69347fc89c23eb969cf97d24350b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/7150b8a371ee69347fc89c23eb969cf97d24350b"}],"sha":"8c3de69ced5049a2d02cdf6520b8e08ec9f1035f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/8c3de69ced5049a2d02cdf6520b8e08ec9f1035f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6631578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shpilevoy","id":6631578,"login":"shpilevoy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzE1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/7150b8a371ee69347fc89c23eb969cf97d24350b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T15:39:55Z","email":"nick@shpil.io","name":"Nikita Shpilevoy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T15:39:55Z","email":"nick@shpil.io","name":"Nikita Shpilevoy"},"message":"refactor(healthex): finish reconcile migration — drop in-process HealthEx from routes\n\nCompletes the migration started in the previous commit. In-process\nconsent-state reconciliation is fully owned by the healthex_reconcile\nDAG (in healthkey-etl); fhir-importers routes are now storage/trigger\nonly.\n\nBackend:\n- poll_status collapses from ~130 lines to ~15: return the DB row,\n  refresh last_status_polled_at, done. No get_consent_state call, no\n  get_data_retrieval_status call. Explicit regression test asserts\n  neither client method is invoked (autospec assert_not_called).\n- Delete the dead _map_upstream_status helper and its status-enum\n  imports (STATUS_COMPLETE/ERROR/RETRIEVAL_IN_PROGRESS) that were only\n  used by the removed data-retrieval-status polling.\n- HealthExClient.get_consent_state stays — cli/patient.py find still\n  uses it for operator debug.\n\nFrontend:\n- HealthExConnections on-mount: swap per-row getStatus fan-out for\n  per-row reconcile fan-out + bounded listConnections polling (5\n  attempts × 3s, stops early once every row''s last_status_polled_at\n  advances). Sees revocations and fresh OPTED_IN rows without waiting\n  on the periodic DAG tick.\n- ConnectHealthEx polling loop: fire reconcile once at start so the\n  DAG updates the row while getStatus polls the DB.\n- New reconcile() method on HealthExClient TS interface +\n  HealthExReconcileResult type. Same POST shape as ingest().\n\nTests (3 new):\n- /status returns DB state with autospec assert_not_called guards on\n  both HealthExClient methods (get_consent_state, get_data_retrieval_status).\n- /status advances polled_at on every call (frontend depends on this\n  as its ''DAG finished'' signal).\n- /status 404 when no link.\n\nDeploy ordering: healthkey-etl DAG must be running before this ships,\notherwise /reconcile fires an Airflow dag_run against a nonexistent\ndag_id and returns 502. Since the periodic DAG tick already covers the\n''user doesn''t visit the page for 30 min'' case, the failure mode of\nshipping this ahead of the DAG is ''callback-flow reconciliation is\nbroken'' — visible in Sentry via the ''Failed to trigger healthex_reconcile\nDAG'' logger.exception on each /reconcile call.\n\nFull suite: 67 passing (was 64).","tree":{"sha":"28aece10b1dafd84cf17cb602a7f3907224a922a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/git/trees/28aece10b1dafd84cf17cb602a7f3907224a922a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/git/commits/7150b8a371ee69347fc89c23eb969cf97d24350b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6631578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shpilevoy","id":6631578,"login":"shpilevoy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzE1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commit/7150b8a371ee69347fc89c23eb969cf97d24350b","node_id":"C_kwDOSaMNktoAKDcxNTBiOGEzNzFlZTY5MzQ3ZmM4OWMyM2ViOTY5Y2Y5N2QyNDM1MGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commit/d2744256e63f45ee507c10843261e09634161ba4","sha":"d2744256e63f45ee507c10843261e09634161ba4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/d2744256e63f45ee507c10843261e09634161ba4"}],"sha":"7150b8a371ee69347fc89c23eb969cf97d24350b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/7150b8a371ee69347fc89c23eb969cf97d24350b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6631578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shpilevoy","id":6631578,"login":"shpilevoy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzE1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/d2744256e63f45ee507c10843261e09634161ba4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T15:31:52Z","email":"nick@shpil.io","name":"Nikita Shpilevoy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T15:31:52Z","email":"nick@shpil.io","name":"Nikita Shpilevoy"},"message":"feat(healthex): POST /connections/{project_id}/reconcile fires healthex_reconcile DAG\n\nFhir-importers side of the reconcile procedure that the healthkey-etl\nhealthex_reconcile DAG owns. Frontend will call this from the callback\nflow (on connections-page mount, per-row) to force a HealthEx ground-\ntruth check without waiting on the periodic DAG schedule.\n\n- Distinct from /ingest: not gated on healthex_patient_id, since reconcile\n  is precisely how a PENDING_CONSENT row discovers its patient_id. Conf\n  passed to Airflow is minimal ({user_uid, project_id}) — the DAG derives\n  everything else from getPatientConsents + the healthex_patient_links row.\n- 502 detail is generic (''Airflow trigger failed''); internal URL goes to\n  Sentry via logger.exception. Same pattern as /ingest.\n\nTwo-phase rollout is deliberate:\n- Phase 1 (this commit): endpoint + tests. In-process reconcile in\n  poll_status stays live so we don''t lose coverage during the healthkey-etl\n  deploy gap.\n- Phase 2 (follow-up PR after DAG verified in prod): rewire\n  HealthExConnections.tsx to fan out /reconcile per row instead of\n  /status; delete in-process reconcile from poll_status; keep\n  get_consent_state for CLI use.\n\nTests (5, all passing):\n- Happy path with resolved patient_id -> 202, correct DAG conf shape,\n  right dag name, dag_run_prefix.\n- Happy path with patient_id=None -> DAG STILL triggered (primary\n  callback-flow scenario; guards against a future maintainer adding a\n  409 gate here by mistake).\n- 404 when no link.\n- 502 on AirflowError with generic detail; regression asserting\n  ''airflow.internal'' does not appear in the response body.\n- 401 when no bearer token.\n\nFull suite: 64 passed (was 59).","tree":{"sha":"12815e2eb31126f3ef62ac82be199585d832a23d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/git/trees/12815e2eb31126f3ef62ac82be199585d832a23d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/git/commits/d2744256e63f45ee507c10843261e09634161ba4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6631578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shpilevoy","id":6631578,"login":"shpilevoy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzE1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commit/d2744256e63f45ee507c10843261e09634161ba4","node_id":"C_kwDOSaMNktoAKGQyNzQ0MjU2ZTYzZjQ1ZWU1MDdjMTA4NDMyNjFlMDk2MzQxNjFiYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commit/3f45bfdcfb67272f59372870b601ba053aaf36b1","sha":"3f45bfdcfb67272f59372870b601ba053aaf36b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/3f45bfdcfb67272f59372870b601ba053aaf36b1"}],"sha":"d2744256e63f45ee507c10843261e09634161ba4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/d2744256e63f45ee507c10843261e09634161ba4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6631578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shpilevoy","id":6631578,"login":"shpilevoy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzE1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/3f45bfdcfb67272f59372870b601ba053aaf36b1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T14:28:42Z","email":"nick@shpil.io","name":"Nikita Shpilevoy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T14:28:42Z","email":"nick@shpil.io","name":"Nikita Shpilevoy"},"message":"test(healthex): cover get_consent_state (getPatientConsents) parsing\n\nDiego''s revocation reconciliation depends on the three-state distinction\nreturned by get_consent_state — but there was zero coverage on the\nparsing path. tests/test_healthex_routes.py autospecs HealthExClient so\nit never exercises real HTTP or JSON parsing; tests/test_healthex_client_live.py\nonly hits /v1/auth/token and /FHIR/R4/metadata.\n\nFills the gap with httpx.MockTransport-based unit tests. Ten cases\nacross five buckets:\n\n1. OPTED_IN PATIENT_DIRECTED_DATA_EXCHANGE -> patient_id populated,\n   known_by_healthex=True. Also asserts the outbound call hits\n   /v1/patients/consents with externalId+projectId params.\n2. Non-OPTED_IN PATIENT_DIRECTED_DATA_EXCHANGE (parametrised over\n   OPTED_OUT/REVOKED/WITHDRAWN) -> patient_id=None, known_by_healthex=True.\n   This is the case poll_status uses to fire REVOKED.\n3. Pending: empty results, 400 ''Patient not found'', and 400 with an\n   unfamiliar short body (must log WARNING per the vendor-copy-drift\n   guard in the client).\n4. Other consent types (MARKETING/RESEARCH) must not mark the externalId\n   as known — regression guard against poll_status incorrectly firing\n   REVOKED when a user has a non-DATA_EXCHANGE consent on record.\n5. 5xx and non-JSON bodies raise HealthExError.\n\nUses httpx.MockTransport rather than adding respx as a new dep — one\nless thing to install and Python-stdlib-adjacent enough for a small\naudit surface.","tree":{"sha":"a2f4926fda2d50c2c71e2ba9b8ce5e2841387d08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/git/trees/a2f4926fda2d50c2c71e2ba9b8ce5e2841387d08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/git/commits/3f45bfdcfb67272f59372870b601ba053aaf36b1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6631578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shpilevoy","id":6631578,"login":"shpilevoy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzE1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commit/3f45bfdcfb67272f59372870b601ba053aaf36b1","node_id":"C_kwDOSaMNktoAKDNmNDViZmRjZmI2NzI3MmY1OTM3Mjg3MGI2MDFiYTA1M2FhZjM2YjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commit/6226c2cd7ef528a5dccc7cfb6beb799ee9a2c904","sha":"6226c2cd7ef528a5dccc7cfb6beb799ee9a2c904","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/6226c2cd7ef528a5dccc7cfb6beb799ee9a2c904"}],"sha":"3f45bfdcfb67272f59372870b601ba053aaf36b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/3f45bfdcfb67272f59372870b601ba053aaf36b1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6631578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shpilevoy","id":6631578,"login":"shpilevoy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzE1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/6226c2cd7ef528a5dccc7cfb6beb799ee9a2c904/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T14:18:57Z","email":"nick@shpil.io","name":"Nikita Shpilevoy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T14:18:57Z","email":"nick@shpil.io","name":"Nikita Shpilevoy"},"message":"feat(healthex): reconcile REVOKED consent from HealthEx on status poll\n\nDiego''s ask: ''if somebody uses HealthEx UI to delete [a consent] — how\nare you going to keep the HealthEx state with yours?''. Today, we don''t.\nOnce a row has a healthex_patient_id our poll_status endpoint stops\nchecking getPatientConsents, so a HealthEx-side revocation never\nsurfaces in the HT UI.\n\nBackend:\n- services/healthex_client.py: replace find_patient_id_by_external_id\n  with get_consent_state → HealthExConsentState dataclass that\n  distinguishes ''no record'' (pending) from ''record exists but not\n  OPTED_IN'' (revoked). The old method collapsed both to None.\n- app/healthex_routers.py:poll_status: call get_consent_state on EVERY\n  poll (not just when patient_id is None). If we had a patient_id and\n  HealthEx now reports the record isn''t OPTED_IN → flip row to REVOKED.\n  Extra ~200-500ms per poll; acceptable for a rare-ish page.\n- cli/patient.py: ''patient find'' CLI now distinguishes ''pending'' vs\n  ''revoked'' in its output.\n\nFrontend:\n- HealthExConnections.tsx: on mount, after listConnections(), fan-out\n  getStatus() per row with patient_id set. That''s a client-side\n  reconcile: the backend re-hits HealthEx and REVOKED lands in the row\n  the user sees. Fire-and-forget; original list renders immediately,\n  refreshed rows land in second render.\n\nExplicitly NOT covered here (still gaps):\n- Consents created directly on HealthEx UI without going through our\n  /connect — we won''t see them until a background reconciler exists.\n- Row state that changes between page loads (user isn''t watching) —\n  same. Long-term needs a scheduled DAG or webhook from HealthEx.","tree":{"sha":"e8c0280ad4e856266d5a95280afff84791d5f0dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/git/trees/e8c0280ad4e856266d5a95280afff84791d5f0dd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/git/commits/6226c2cd7ef528a5dccc7cfb6beb799ee9a2c904","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"