"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T14:26:03Z","email":"nick@shpil.io","name":"Nikita Shpilevoy"},"message":"test(healthex): first @external_api test — live HealthEx smoke\n\nThree cheapest-possible integration checks that don''t touch a real\npatient or mutate any project state:\n\n- org_jwt(): mint the 24h org token — proves base_url/api_key/api_secret/\n  project_id all line up with what the vendor''s side has provisioned.\n- jwt_claims(): decoded payload carries a UUID-shaped organizationId\n  (needed for cross-service trace correlation; guards against format\n  drift, not the specific value, since sandbox and prod will differ).\n- get_capability_statement(): FHIR endpoint accepts our bearer token\n  and speaks R4. Catches a broken FHIR-side deploy without a real pull.\n\npytest.ini + pyproject.toml:\n- Consolidated all pytest config into pytest.ini — bare pytest.ini\n  files take precedence over [tool.pytest.ini_options] in pyproject.toml\n  and were silently dropping asyncio_mode/testpaths (which made the\n  new async tests fail with ''async functions not natively supported''\n  and collection walk into examples/).\n- Default addopts excludes external_api and llm markers so make pytest\n  stays free of the wire and quota-consuming markers. Opt in with\n  ''pytest -m external_api''.\n\nCLAUDE.md: (change carried in — the testing chapter now already\ndocuments the marker split; no additional edits needed.)","tree":{"sha":"8f65ea9360be18378b232366af6dd576afe4e81f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/git/trees/8f65ea9360be18378b232366af6dd576afe4e81f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/git/commits/3e9df24d42f2414f41cd11e4c82622bc180a4b26","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6631578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/events{/privacy}"