ey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/8fbd18a9cea48939d345a38663cfd19048d3efc4"}],"sha":"057a8066c34dbd9e5fc6628cb020e94683cac25b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/057a8066c34dbd9e5fc6628cb020e94683cac25b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6631578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shpilevoy","id":6631578,"login":"shpilevoy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzE1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/commits/8fbd18a9cea48939d345a38663cfd19048d3efc4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T01:22:01Z","email":"nick@shpil.io","name":"Nikita Shpilevoy"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T01:22:01Z","email":"nick@shpil.io","name":"Nikita Shpilevoy"},"message":"fix: post-deploy review cleanups\n\n- auth: split blanket except into ExpiredIdTokenError/RevokedIdTokenError/\n  InvalidIdTokenError (401 with distinct details) + catch-all (503 with\n  exception log). Project-id mismatch and JWKS-fetch failures are now\n  visible instead of masquerading as ''invalid token from client''.\n- healthex_routers: replace three ''assert updated is not None'' with\n  HTTPException(409). python -O would strip the asserts and let an\n  AttributeError surface deeper down.\n- healthex_client: widen the getPatientConsents 400 sentinel to ''any 400\n  with short body'', log a warning when wording is unfamiliar — vendor\n  copy change no longer silently coerces real errors to pending-consent.\n- ConnectHealthEx: hydrate the oldest connection (deterministic) instead\n  of conns[0] (server-order dependent). Future-proofs for multi-project.\n- deploy.yml: poll docker compose ps for up to 30s after up -d\n  --force-recreate; dump --tail=200 logs and fail the job if the app\n  container is restarting/exited. The next services/-style\n  ModuleNotFoundError will fail loudly instead of slipping through to\n  smoke.\n- deploy/docker-compose.yaml: drop the dead ''migrate'' service; comment\n  points to the workflow which runs migrations via the app image.\n- .dockerignore: add tests/ and frontend/.env* (with .env.example\n  carve-out) so test code and frontend secrets don''t enter the build\n  context Google Cloud Build uploads.","tree":{"sha":"303ef57cfee365c99dec37320f4ec5de9938cd0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/git/trees/303ef57cfee365c99dec37320f4ec5de9938cd0b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/healthkey-ai/fhir_importers/git/commits/8fbd18a9cea48939d345a38663cfd19048d3efc4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6631578?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shpilevoy","id":6631578,"login":"shpilevoy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzE1Nzg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shpilevoy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://a