mmitter":{"date":"2026-05-22T05:41:12Z","email":"gio.rombus@gmail.com","name":"romer8"},"message":"chore(changelog): finalize 0.5.0\n\nEight PRs from the 2026-05-21 popup-modal arc, grouped into Added /\nChanged / Fixed / Tests / Documentation per Keep a Changelog. New tool\n+ slash-prompt for configure_popup_modal_layer (PR #10), case-fold\nargs normalization for popup gridItems + render_plugin +\nadd_dynamic_map_layer (PRs #14 + #15), ESRI sublayer-ID extraction\nfrom LAYERDEFS + ESRI Image guard widening (PRs #12 + #17), WMS\nattr_key from wms_layers (PR #16), popup_options outer-key\nnormalization across all 11 add_*_layer tools (PR #11), tool\ndescription tightening for case-sensitive arg_names + 100-col grid\n(PR #13). Suite grew 930 → 961.","tree":{"sha":"16ba09de1d413f6ee929b0ac54ddb52e5b44d0a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/trees/16ba09de1d413f6ee929b0ac54ddb52e5b44d0a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/commits/89aaaf2e3cd32f0325db50e96fe0e40913752418","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43544549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/romer8","id":43544549,"login":"romer8","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQ0NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commit/89aaaf2e3cd32f0325db50e96fe0e40913752418","node_id":"C_kwDOSajnbNoAKDg5YWFhZjJlM2NkMzJmMDMyNWRiNTBlOTZmZTBlNDA5MTM3NTI0MTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commit/1c722d9bb01e92bca1a9a1455ce10cf85f46fbd9","sha":"1c722d9bb01e92bca1a9a1455ce10cf85f46fbd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/1c722d9bb01e92bca1a9a1455ce10cf85f46fbd9"}],"sha":"89aaaf2e3cd32f0325db50e96fe0e40913752418","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/89aaaf2e3cd32f0325db50e96fe0e40913752418"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43544549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/romer8","id":43544549,"login":"romer8","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQ0NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/1c722d9bb01e92bca1a9a1455ce10cf85f46fbd9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-22T02:32:16Z","email":"43544549+romer8@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Gio"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-22T02:32:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(tools): widen ESRI Image attr_key resolution to fire for popup_options too (#17)\n\nDebug audit 2026-05-21 secondary finding: add_esri_image_layer''s\nattr_key resolution (PR #12) was gated on `if attribute_variables:`.\nThe popup_options-alone case fell through with the display-name\nfallback, causing silent click-time misses in the popup-table render\npath.\n\nServer side (mcp_server.py:2061): `if attribute_variables:` triggered\nthe _resolve_esri_layer_name call. popup_options provided WITHOUT\nattribute_variables left attr_key = name (display name).\n\nReact side (utilities.js getImageArcGISRestLayerAttributes): keys\nalias maps by the service-side layer.name fetched from ?f=json —\nsame as the attribute_variables path. So popup_options.{aliases,omit}\nkeyed by display name would silently miss at lookup time.\n\nPR #11''s outer-key normalization rewrites popup_options.{aliases,omit}\nto attr_key. With attr_key=display_name, that rewrote to the wrong\nkey.\n\nWiden the guard from `if attribute_variables:` to\n`if attribute_variables or popup_options:`. The resolver is a\nsoft-fail (returns None on network failure → fallback to display name\npreserved). Inline comment expanded to explain both code paths and\nthe React popup-render contract.\n\nNo new helper or behavior change for the attribute_variables case —\njust makes the existing resolution machinery fire for one more\ncondition.\n\n5 new in TestAddEsriImagePopupOptionsAttrKeyResolution:\n- test_popup_options_aliases_alone_uses_resolved_sublayer_name: the\n  motivating case — popup_options.aliases alone, outer key rewritten\n  to resolved sublayer name, not display name\n- test_popup_options_omit_alone_uses_resolved_sublayer_name: same for\n  the omit field\n- test_both_attribute_variables_and_popup_options_same_attr_key:\n  defensive — both fields keyed by the same resolved sublayer name\n- test_popup_options_alone_resolver_fails_falls_back_to_display_name:\n  soft-fail path preserved\n- test_neither_attribute_variables_nor_popup_options_no_resolver_call:\n  regression — when neither field is provided, resolver doesn''t fire\n  (no wasted network call)\n\nFull suite: 949 passed (944 baseline + 5 new).\n\nThis is the 8th PR in the 2026-05-21 debug arc. Class A surface for\nESRI Image now fully covered — the original PR #12 fix for\nattribute_variables + this PR for popup_options. Combined with PR #16\n(WMS attr_key from wms_layers), all known Class A bugs are addressed.\n\nESRI Feature / GeoJSON / KML / tile types / GeoTIFF / static image\nremain not-affected (caller-supplied layerName matches across server\n+ React, or are not queryable at the attribute level).","tree":{"sha":"270263f769086d39ec9eaa7283ae5ed84b070805","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/trees/270263f769086d39ec9eaa7283ae5ed84b070805"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/commits/1c722d9bb01e92bca1a9a1455ce10cf85f46fbd9","verification":{"payload":"tree 270263f769086d39ec9eaa7283ae5ed84b070805\nparent c70295bdcd3da97d36848fe0b5b608888bce6e29\nauthor Gio <43544549+romer8@users.noreply.github.com> 1779417136 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779417136 -0600\n\nfix(tools): widen ESRI Image attr_key resolution to fire for popup_options too (#17)\n\nDebug audit 2026-05-21 secondary finding: add_esri_image_layer''s\nattr_key resolution (PR #12) was gated on `if attribute_variables:`.\nThe popup_options-alone case fell through with the display-name\nfallback, causing silent click-time misses in the popup-table render\npath.\n\nServer side (mcp_server.py:2061): `if attribute_variables:` triggered\nthe _resolve_esri_layer_name call. popup_options provided WITHOUT\nattribute_variables left attr_key = name (display name).\n\nReact side (utilities.js getImageArcGISRestLayerAttributes): keys\nalias maps by the service-side layer.name fetched from ?f=json —\nsame as the attribute_variables path. So popup_options.{aliases,omit}\nkeyed by display name would silently miss at lookup time.\n\nPR #11''s outer-key normalization rewrites popup_options.{aliases,omit}\nto attr_key. With attr_key=display_name, that rewrote to the wrong\nkey.\n\nWiden the guard from `if attribute_variables:` to\n`if attribute_variables or popup_options:`. The resolver is a\nsoft-fail (returns None on network failure → fallback to display name\npreserved). Inline comment expanded to explain both code paths and\nthe React popup-render contract.\n\nNo new helper or behavior change for the attribute_variables case —\njust makes the existing resolution machinery fire for one more\ncondition.\n\n5 new in TestAddEsriImagePopupOptionsAttrKeyResolution:\n- test_popup_options_aliases_alone_uses_resolved_sublayer_name: the\n  motivating case — popup_options.aliases alone, outer key rewritten\n  to resolved sublayer name, not display name\n- test_popup_options_omit_alone_uses_resolved_sublayer_name: same for\n  the omit field\n- test_both_attribute_variables_and_popup_options_same_attr_key:\n  defensive — both fields keyed by the same resolved sublayer name\n- test_popup_options_alone_resolver_fails_falls_back_to_display_name:\n  soft-fail path preserved\n- test_neither_attribute_variables_nor_popup_options_no_resolver_call:\n  regression — when neither field is provided, resolver doesn''t fire\n  (no wasted network call)\n\nFull suite: 949 passed (944 baseline + 5 new).\n\nThis is the 8th PR in the 2026-05-21 debug arc. Class A surface for\nESRI Image now fully covered — the original PR #12 fix for\nattribute_variables + this PR for popup_options. Combined with PR #16\n(WMS attr_key from wms_layers), all known Class A bugs are addressed.\n\nESRI Feature / GeoJSON / KML / tile types / GeoTIFF / static image\nremain not-affected (caller-supplied layerName matches across server\n+ React, or are not queryable at the attribute level).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqD8AwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfAEQAG9aqdl/bAlDaS4ydMv3bB+0\nsWxumpR7JFW6ui7d