bdd736e75b"}],"sha":"4457fe62a4f24c3e59bbd6ef702a160cb16b9288","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/4457fe62a4f24c3e59bbd6ef702a160cb16b9288"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43544549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/romer8","id":43544549,"login":"romer8","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQ0NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/8d2a4da9385a72f2904e96938f413abdd736e75b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-21T22:22:56Z","email":"43544549+romer8@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Gio"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-21T22:22:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(tools): name aliases/omit keys in popup_options descriptions on all add_*_layer tools (#11)\n\n* chore: strip plan references from code comments\n\nComments in mcp_server.py and plugin_helpers.py referenced ''Plan 2026-XX-YYY''\ndocuments that no longer add value to a reader of the code. Per the project''s\n\"no comments referencing the current task or PR\" convention, replace them\nwith comments that explain the WHY of the surrounding code without mentioning\nthe plan that introduced it.\n\nNo behavior change. Comment-only edits.\n\n* fix(tools): name aliases/omit keys in popup_options descriptions on all add_*_layer tools\n\nDebug session 2026-05-21: gemini-flash misrouted \"alias the comid\nattribute to River ID\" to attribute_variables on add_esri_image_layer\ninstead of popup_options.aliases. Root cause: 10 of 11 add_*_layer\ntools shipped with a 3-word stub description for popup_options\n(\"Click-popup options\") that named neither the aliases nor omit keys,\nwhile attribute_variables sat next to it with a 35-word description\nmentioning \"feature attribute names\" 3 times — strong semantic match\nfor \"alias attribute\". The LLM picked the field whose description\ncarried the relevant domain idiom.\n\nadd_wms_layer was the lone outlier with the full description naming\nboth sub-keys. This commit lockstep-replaces the stub across the\nremaining 10 tools (add_esri_image_layer, add_esri_feature_layer,\nadd_geojson_layer, add_kml_layer, add_image_tile_layer,\nadd_vector_tile_layer, add_pmtiles_vector_layer,\nadd_pmtiles_raster_layer, add_geotiff_layer, add_static_image_layer)\nwith the same wording add_wms_layer already has, so all 11 popup-\ncapable layer tools now describe popup_options identically.\n\nAdds test_mcp/test_popup_options_description_drift.py — 22\nparametrized assertions (11 tools × 2 keywords) that pin the wording\nso future edits can''t silently drop the aliases or omit keywords. The\ntest reads descriptions via the FastMCP catalog (mcp._local_provider.\nlist_tools()), mirroring test_tool_description_exclusivity.py''s\npattern.\n\nNo behavior change. Full suite: 861 tests pass (839 prior + 22 new).\n\n* fix(tools): tolerate wrong popup_options outer key + tighten description binding\n\nDebug session 2026-05-21 turn 1 with gemini-flash: the LLM emitted\n`popup_options.aliases = {\"0\": {\"comid\": \"River ID\"}}` on an ESRI\nImage layer call. The \"0\" came from the user prompt''s\n`params.LAYERDEFS = \"0:rivercountry = ''China''\"` — the model conflated\nthe sublayer index with the outer-key shape''s `layer_name` slot. The\nserver accepted the call and stored the alias under key \"0\", but the\nReact popup-render path (`Map.js:641-650`) keys alias maps by layer\nNAME, so the alias silently never fired at click time. User-visible\nbug: popup table showed \"comid\" instead of \"River ID\".\n\nTwo fixes layered onto PR #11''s description-drift work:\n\n1. **Server-side tolerance** — `_normalize_popup_outer_keys` in\n   `_apply_common_layer_options`: when `popup_options.aliases` or\n   `.omit` is a single-entry dict whose outer key doesn''t match the\n   layer''s `name` arg, rewrite the key to `name`. Catches the\n   sublayer-ID case AND the literal \"layer_name\" placeholder case.\n   Multi-entry dicts pass through unchanged (caller''s apparent intent\n   of cross-layer authoring is respected). Logs the rewrite at DEBUG\n   so it''s grep-able if it ever surprises a caller.\n\n2. **Description anchoring** — extend the description PR #11 lockstep-\n   updated on all 11 `add_*_layer` tools'' `popup_options` field: name\n   the binding explicitly (\"outer layer_name key MUST be the same\n   string passed as this tool''s `name` arg — NOT a sublayer ID from\n   params, params.LAYERDEFS, layer_id, or any other identifier\"). Per\n   `feedback_input_output_name_alignment.md` — description text is\n   the LLM''s primary signal.\n\nTests:\n- 6 new tests in TestPopupOptionsOuterKeyNormalization\n  (test_per_source_type_layer_tools.py): single-entry rewrite,\n  matching-key preserved, literal-placeholder rewrite, omit\n  normalization symmetry, multi-entry preserved, empty no-op.\n- 11 new parametrized assertions in\n  test_popup_options_description_drift.py asserting the\n  `\\`name\\` arg` anchor text appears on every add_*_layer''s\n  popup_options description.\n\nFull suite: 878 passed (zero regressions).","tree":{"sha":"a94051b91e95429f06bfeac1ba14db82f035af90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/trees/a94051b91e95429f06bfeac1ba14db82f035af90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/commits/8d2a4da9385a72f2904e96938f413abdd736e75b","verification":{"payload":"tree a94051b91e95429f06bfeac1ba14db82f035af90\nparent ed0e9704d69a09d181525e8385cb7d8a843bdb06\nauthor Gio <43544549+romer8@users.noreply.github.com> 1779402176 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779402176 -0600\n\nfix(tools): name aliases/omit keys in popup_options descriptions on all add_*_layer tools (#11)\n\n* chore: strip plan references from code comments\n\nComments in mcp_server.py and plugin_helpers.py referenced ''Plan 2026-XX-YYY''\ndocuments that no longer add value to a reader of the code. Per the project''s\n\"no comments referencing the current task or PR\" convention, replace them\nwith comments that explain the WHY of the surrounding code without mentioning\nthe plan that introduced it.\n\nNo behavior change. Comment-only edits.\n\n* fix(tools): name aliases/omit keys in popup_options descriptions on all add_*_layer tools\n\nDebug session 2026-05-21: gemini-flash misrouted \"alias the comid\nattribute to River ID\" to attribute_variables on add_esri_image_layer\ninstead of popup_options.aliases. Root cause: 10 of 11 add_*_layer\ntools shipped with a 3-word stub description for popup_options\n(\"Click-popup options\") that named neither the aliases nor omit keys,\nwhile attribute_variables sat next to it with a 35-word description\nmentioning \"feature attribute names\" 3 times — strong semantic match\nfor \"alias attribute\". The LLM picked the field whose description\ncarried the relevant domain idiom.\n\nadd_wms_layer was the lone outlier with the full description naming\nboth sub-keys. This commit lockstep-replaces the stub across the\nremaining 10 tools (add_esri_image_layer, add_esri_feature_layer,\nadd_geojson_layer, add_kml_layer, add_image_tile_layer,\nadd_vector_tile_layer, add_pmtiles_vector_layer,\nadd_pmtiles_raster_layer, add_geotiff_layer, add_static_image_layer)\nwith the same wording add_wms_layer already has, so all 11 popup-\ncapable layer tools now describe popup_options identically.\n\nAdds test_mcp/test_popup_options_description_drift.py — 22\nparametrized assertions (11 tools × 2 keywords) that pin the wording\nso future edits can''t silently drop the aliases or omit keywords. The\ntest reads descriptions via the FastMCP catalog (mcp._local_provider.\nlist_tools()), mirroring test_tool_description_exclusivity.py''s\npattern.\n\nNo behavior change. Full suite: 861 tests pass (839 prior + 22 new).\n\n* fix(tools): tolerate wrong popup_options outer key + tighten description binding\n\nDebug session 2026-05-21 turn 1 with gemini-flash: the LLM emitted\n`popup_options.aliases = {\"0\": {\"comid\": \"River ID\"}}` on an ESRI\nImage layer call. The \"0\" came from the user prompt''s\n`params.LAYERDEFS = \"0:rivercountry = ''China''\"` — the model conflated\nthe sublayer index with the outer-key shape''s `layer_name` slot. The\nserver accepted the call and stored the alias under key \"0\", but the\nReact popup-render path (`Map.js:641-650`) keys alias maps by layer\nNAME, so the alias silently never fired at click time. User-visible\nbug: popup table showed \"comid\" instead of \"River ID\".\n\nTwo fixes layered onto PR #11''s description-drift work:\n\n1. **Server-side tolerance** — `_normalize_popup_outer_keys` in\n   `_apply_common_layer_options`: when `popup_options.aliases` or\n   `.omit` is a single-entry dict whose outer key doesn''t match the\n   layer''s `name` arg, rewrite the key to `name`. Catches the\n   sublayer-ID case AND the literal \"layer_name\" placeholder case.\n   Multi-entry dicts pass through unchanged (caller''s apparent intent\n   of cross-layer authoring is respected). Logs the rewrite at DEBUG\n   so it''s grep-able if it ever surprises a caller.\n\n2. **Description anchoring** — extend the description PR #11 lockstep-\n   updated on all 11 `add_*_layer` tools'' `popup_options` field: name\n   the binding explicitly (\"outer layer_name key MUST be the same\n   string passed as this tool''s `name` arg — NOT a sublayer ID from\n   params, params.LAYERDEFS, layer_id, or any other identifier\"). Per\n   `feedback_input_output_name_alignment.md` — description text is\n   the LLM''s primary signal.\n\nTests:\n- 6 new tests in TestPopupOptionsOuterKeyNormalization\n  (test_per_source_type_layer_tools.py): single-entry rewrite,\n  matching-key preserved, literal-placeholder rewrite, omit\n  normalization symmetry, multi-entry preserved, empty no-op.\n- 11 new parametrized assertions in\n  test_popup_options_description_drift.py asserting the\n  `\\`name\\` arg` anchor text appears on every add_*_layer''s\n  popup_options description.\n\nFull suite: 878 passed (zero regressions).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqD4XACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6qsQAHi3IaUKionq1pAUpCmcZDwG\nODCYD8kDuqVWcM85HZQL2HD7zmW8kuHcc+wLeWKu6dOFH6Qp2zXa3CQZZ0hP50zY\ndOWhpH8lm5andRmIR7cL8whp3aNi8t4NXa7YpLQxJMmlOJf5B4qjTYden4TB6d5E\na36SRtMaz6Y8MTL47OW5L0D/wsaXNDTejdo5fES4fidU/Z5+5J+9Y9irP9u8o8/u\npQ5ypYUIkhAmROnZRpKYT+NWEpegzcL4JbmNplIQZ3XnLcxlk76XpOiQ4p+8F5o6\nRuynVNnvzC+FRxFuZmxs4R4G678A7DtjOoTzzoW8SAiqMnYXJLu4S8Cio6c06wYB\nQ+SQ+uaizA/m20O9x+G+fAFUMV20I8OPtleuW4xkBTm0/EdcViIahBj1thcwXri6\nGQqh9r/fuGxZDtjVvouiK0k2WAi/vOk9UQQvtBWm/RNAg9lgxlytC0tvNyqRY5FL\nTc10ocs38NZisxTppo/XnDARPKjWtcbTVyAWNrjpWTcE6j60JbbDZFvRhxbbj8f4\nEufzEYnEsToGXS559kD5zNC4cFkeBUpiRdjBBQulcjW1kbEXy7s7r4VGJ6qpkpAi\nJHM/KlyCSsG2eY2cJMKpa7frlqPGd4vZArpJ9suESsoB14lcCuLfs0myzB0YBKTB\nVGHPl7YWoo/rQcjpABuB\n=eE6l\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-21T22:22:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commit/8d2a4da9385a72f2904e96938f413abdd736e75b","node_id":"C_kwDOSajnbNoAKDhkMmE0ZGE5Mzg1YTcyZjI5MDRlOTY5MzhmNDEzYWJkZDczNmU3NWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commit/ed0e9704d69a09d181525e8385cb7d8a843bdb06","sha":"ed0e9704d69a09d181525e8385cb7d8a843bdb06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/ed0e9704d69a09d181525e8385cb7d8a843bdb06"}],"sha":"8d2a4da9385a72f2904e96938f413abdd736e75b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/8d2a4da9385a72f2904e96938f413abdd736e75b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43544549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/romer8","id":43544549,"login":"romer8","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQ0NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/ed0e9704d69a09d181525e8385cb7d8a843bdb06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-21T04:24:29Z","email":"43544549+romer8@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Gio"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-21T04:24:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(tools): tighten data field descriptions from PREFER to imperative MUST (#9)\n\nTouches create_plotly_chart / create_data_table / create_card.\n\nThe PREFER framing was soft enough that gemini-3-flash-preview and\nnemotron-3-nano-30b both READ the rule in their thinking traces,\nrationalized inline data as \"small enough\", and tokenized 24 rows\nverbatim into the next tool call — wasting 12-37s of LLM output\nemission per turn (debug session 2026-05-20). Imperative framing\nanchored on the observable signal (_cache_uri in any recent tool\nresult) gives the LLM a concrete rule rather than a judgment call.\n\nSmoke tested 2026-05-20: nemotron-3-nano:30b with thinking disabled\nemitted data_uri=\"mcp+cache://...\" on first try after the tightening,\nno inline data.\n\nThe existing 4-assertion test contract still passes (data_uri named,\n_cache_uri named, data_uri before Inline shape, small-model failure\nmode named). 2 new assertions lock in:\n- imperative `MUST use \\`data_uri\\`` framing, with `PREFER` absent\n- rule anchored on \"recent tool result\" signal (not unconditional)\n\n18/18 description tests pass, 839/839 full suite passes.","tree":{"sha":"91076bb5970c551e2ef843202354e1cd6d5f7f94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/trees/91076bb5970c551e2ef843202354e1cd6d5f7f94"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/commits/ed0e9704d69a09d181525e8385cb7d8a843bdb06","verification":{"payload":"tree 91076bb5970c551e2ef843202354e1cd6d5f7f94\nparent a8075514e3e54ddf868dba12d922daef5b182239\nauthor Gio <43544549+romer8@users.noreply.github.com> 1779337469 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779337469 -0600\n\nfix(tools): tighten data field descriptions from PREFER to imperative MUST (#9)\n\nTouches create_plotly_chart / create_data_table / create_card.\n\nThe PREFER framing was soft enough that gemini-3-flash-preview and\nnemotron-3-nano-30b both READ the rule in their thinking traces,\nrationalized inline data as \"small enough\", and tokenized 24 rows\nverbatim into the next tool call — wasting 12-37s of LLM output\nemission per turn (debug session 2026-05-20). Imperative framing\nanchored on the observable signal (_cache_uri in any recent tool\nresult) gives the LLM a concrete rule rather than a judgment call.\n\nSmoke tested 2026-05-20: nemotron-3-nano:30b with thinking disabled\nemitted data_uri=\"mcp+cache://...\" on first try after the tightening,\nno inline data.\n\nThe existing 4-assertion test contract still passes (data_uri named,\n_cache_uri named, data_uri before Inline shape, small-model failure\nmode named). 2 new assertions lock in:\n- imperative `MUST use \\`data_uri\\`` framing, with `PREFER` absent\n- rule anchored on \"recent tool result\" signal (not unconditional)\n\n18/18 description tests pass, 839/839 full suite passes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDoj+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA49UQAB7xVeuoI8zqVKxLsgGHcubE\n45dGscREYcDxk4w5gScFK17E+1bbMMdlVMN/Vw+vKiy1xlQHMOh6j3CNjSOaoiau\nB6Ai/wWv86AIUzu+gjxoYX/Rwt68rhj6Y/flwnuGRas0z9b3EyGB9VX/CKzwCYyb\n5E13/MYyDrC8S9hboZ/e8v72n5O/Vu0zJEfWCpeclXLAMEE5SL8HLgG2ZLCJ5ysq\nqSyTH0Ah6WeZxQl7LXYyMKP5Yu21VzhzA2KLGXi45dz+PrD1aBdm4lnd7xGI/Z/L\nGmtjbnJx2elyXzeOVAaRf+YevXSRdsxpOXrvHwYrbVmHTAGS+awJcZkn5PetWj3N\nLZ6tc4ZzOViRps56lsyniXUUTDvLAkvbOhyOAWXAtqEscpyEIq5HsROIV4tmfi4E\n6Uob09sY/HP4r+TIe1o6CTnF3V4gh3yiL48/Pp1D3FwiR1roZgpysXqa/ShoqDP5\nS44G