e_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQ0NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commit/a8075514e3e54ddf868dba12d922daef5b182239","node_id":"C_kwDOSajnbNoAKGE4MDc1NTE0ZTNlNTRkZGY4NjhkYmExMmQ5MjJkYWVmNWIxODIyMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commit/66e3c1ddd4588397f1b56d98b1dce299ed4e79ba","sha":"66e3c1ddd4588397f1b56d98b1dce299ed4e79ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/66e3c1ddd4588397f1b56d98b1dce299ed4e79ba"}],"sha":"a8075514e3e54ddf868dba12d922daef5b182239","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/a8075514e3e54ddf868dba12d922daef5b182239"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43544549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/romer8","id":43544549,"login":"romer8","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQ0NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/66e3c1ddd4588397f1b56d98b1dce299ed4e79ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-20T05:03:44Z","email":"43544549+romer8@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Gio"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-20T05:03:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(tools): lead data field descriptions with data_uri preferred path (#8)\n\nCompanion to chatbox-core 0.12.0''s pre-dispatch inline-list cap. The\nchatbox-core cap (INLINE_LIST_MAX_RECORDS=20) is the safety net; this\nPR is the proactive nudge: make the LLM pick data_uri on the first try\nso the cap rarely fires.\n\nSmall models pattern-match on the first option listed in a field\ndescription. With the inline shape leading (\"Array of Plotly trace\nobjects...\" / \"Array of row objects...\"), nemotron-class models\nreliably picked inline `data` even when a cached `_cache_uri` was\navailable — triggering JSON parse errors at the ~1KB threshold\n(observed: nemotron-3-nano-30b on a 24-record NRDS plot, `Extra data:\nline 1 column 1275`, ~200s repair-loop oscillation).\n\nEach `data` field description on create_plotly_chart,\ncreate_data_table, and create_card now opens with a `PREFER data_uri\n...` clause naming `_cache_uri` as the source and the small-model\nfailure mode as the reason. Inline shape moves to a clearly-labeled\n\"Inline shape:\" section after.\n\nNo contract change — inline `data` still accepted for small synthesized\npayloads. Only the description text + ordering changed.\n\nNew regression test `test_data_uri_description_ordering.py` pins the\nframing across all three tools: (a) names `data_uri`, (b) names\n`_cache_uri`, (c) mentions `data_uri` before the inline-shape section,\n(d) names the small-model failure mode. 12 assertions, 833/833 total\ntest suite still green.","tree":{"sha":"cdda1e460aaa3accec7d058efbe82aa8ca44543d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/trees/cdda1e460aaa3accec7d058efbe82aa8ca44543d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/commits/66e3c1ddd4588397f1b56d98b1dce299ed4e79ba","verification":{"payload":"tree cdda1e460aaa3accec7d058efbe82aa8ca44543d\nparent 1cdb7f0c4a4d028d51e10f93334d5261adaac54c\nauthor Gio <43544549+romer8@users.noreply.github.com> 1779253424 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779253424 -0600\n\nfeat(tools): lead data field descriptions with data_uri preferred path (#8)\n\nCompanion to chatbox-core 0.12.0''s pre-dispatch inline-list cap. The\nchatbox-core cap (INLINE_LIST_MAX_RECORDS=20) is the safety net; this\nPR is the proactive nudge: make the LLM pick data_uri on the first try\nso the cap rarely fires.\n\nSmall models pattern-match on the first option listed in a field\ndescription. With the inline shape leading (\"Array of Plotly trace\nobjects...\" / \"Array of row objects...\"), nemotron-class models\nreliably picked inline `data` even when a cached `_cache_uri` was\navailable — triggering JSON parse errors at the ~1KB threshold\n(observed: nemotron-3-nano-30b on a 24-record NRDS plot, `Extra data:\nline 1 column 1275`, ~200s repair-loop oscillation).\n\nEach `data` field description on create_plotly_chart,\ncreate_data_table, and create_card now opens with a `PREFER data_uri\n...` clause naming `_cache_uri` as the source and the small-model\nfailure mode as the reason. Inline shape moves to a clearly-labeled\n\"Inline shape:\" section after.\n\nNo contract change — inline `data` still accepted for small synthesized\npayloads. Only the description text + ordering changed.\n\nNew regression test `test_data_uri_description_ordering.py` pins the\nframing across all three tools: (a) names `data_uri`, (b) names\n`_cache_uri`, (c) mentions `data_uri` before the inline-shape section,\n(d) names the small-model failure mode. 12 assertions, 833/833 total\ntest suite still green.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE----