4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/romer8","id":43544549,"login":"romer8","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQ0NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/f2bd383d50785125bc3e1975927bcaee4692969b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T03:15:00Z","email":"43544549+romer8@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Gio"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T03:15:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: image publishing workflow + standardize port to 9001 (#4)\n\nPlan 2026-05-11-007 — workshop-ready image publishing without Cloud\nRun deploy.\n\n### Primary change: image publishing\n\nAdds .github/workflows/release.yml — ports the release-job half of\nnrds_mcps''s release.yml. Tag-driven (v*), multi-arch\n(linux/amd64+arm64), pushes to ghcr.io/aquaveo/tethysdash-mcps with\nprovenance+sbom attestation and GHA cache. The Cloud Run deploy job\nfrom nrds_mcps is deliberately out of scope; operators run the\npublished image themselves via docker / their preferred deployment.\n\nREADME \"Quick start (Docker)\" splits into \"From the published image\n(recommended)\" (docker run ghcr.io/aquaveo/tethysdash-mcps:latest)\nand \"From source (for contributors)\" (docker build).\n\nCHANGELOG documents the workflow + the one-time package-visibility\nflip the operator does in the GitHub UI after the first tag push.\n\n### Secondary change (incidental, bundled): port 9001\n\nStandardizes the standalone''s default port from 9000 to 9001 across\nDockerfile (ENV MCP_PORT + EXPOSE), mcp_server.py (env-var default\n+ docstring), scripts/setup-mcp.sh, .github/workflows/ci.yml (smoke\ndocker run + healthcheck poll), README runbook step references, and\nthe historical 0.1.0 CHANGELOG entries.\n\nCaveat: 9001 also happens to be the embedded server''s default port.\nThe runbook''s \"both can run simultaneously\" line is now corrected —\noperators running both must override one with MCP_PORT=9002 (or\nsimilar) to avoid the bind collision.\n\n### Workshop consumption path post-merge\n\n  docker run --rm -p 9001:9001 \\\n    -e TETHYSDASH_BASE_URL=https://workshop-tethys.example.com/apps/tethysdash \\\n    ghcr.io/aquaveo/tethysdash-mcps:latest\n\n### What this does NOT do (deferred elsewhere)\n\n- No Cloud Run deploy job — plan 2026-05-10-008 (deferred) covers that\n- No authentication on /mcp — plan 2026-05-11-004 (deferred) covers that\n- No AR remote-repo proxy — plan 2026-05-10-008\n\nPlan: docs/plans/2026-05-11-007-feat-tethysdash-mcps-image-publishing-plan.md\nUnits 1-2. Unit 3 (cut v0.2.0 + smoke) is post-merge operator work.","tree":{"sha":"772b03350879de7ac115e91b444daf3d74e68c69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/trees/772b03350879de7ac115e91b444daf3d74e68c69"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/commits/f2bd383d50785125bc3e1975927bcaee4692969b","verification":{"payload":"tree 772b03350879de7ac115e91b444daf3d74e68c69\nparent 67dfb6c1b9c380f21a24c898f0096b196122484a\nauthor Gio <43544549+romer8@users.noreply.github.com> 1778555700 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778555700 -0600\n\nfeat: image publishing workflow + standardize port to 9001 (#4)\n\nPlan 2026-05-11-007 — workshop-ready image publishing without Cloud\nRun deploy.\n\n### Primary change: image publishing\n\nAdds .github/workflows/release.yml — ports the release-job half of\nnrds_mcps''s release.yml. Tag-driven (v*), multi-arch\n(linux/amd64+arm64), pushes to ghcr.io/aquaveo/tethysdash-mcps with\nprovenance+sbom attestation and GHA cache. The Cloud Run deploy job\nfrom nrds_mcps is deliberately out of scope; operators run the\npublished image themselves via docker / their preferred deployment.\n\nREADME \"Quick start (Docker)\" splits into \"From the published image\n(recommended)\" (docker run ghcr.io/aquaveo/tethysdash-mcps:latest)\nand \"From source (for contributors)\" (docker build).\n\nCHANGELOG documents the workflow + the one-time package-visibility\nflip the operator does in the GitHub UI after the first tag push.\n\n### Secondary change (incidental, bundled): port 9001\n\nStandardizes the standalone''s default port from 9000 to 9001 across\nDockerfile (ENV MCP_PORT + EXPOSE), mcp_server.py (env-var default\n+ docstring), scripts/setup-mcp.sh, .github/workflows/ci.yml (smoke\ndocker run + healthcheck poll), README runbook step references, and\nthe historical 0.1.0 CHANGELOG entries.\n\nCaveat: 9001 also happens to be the embedded server''s default port.\nThe runbook''s \"both can run simultaneously\" line is now corrected —\noperators running both must override one with MCP_PORT=9002 (or\nsimilar) to avoid the bind collision.\n\n### Workshop consumption path post-merge\n\n  docker run --rm -p 9001:9001 \\\n    -e TETHYSDASH_BASE_URL=https://workshop-tethys.example.com/apps/tethysdash \\\n    ghcr.io/aquaveo/tethysdash-mcps:latest\n\n### What this does NOT do (deferred elsewhere)\n\n- No Cloud Run deploy job — plan 2026-05-10-008 (deferred) covers that\n- No authentication on /mcp — plan 2026-05-11-004 (deferred) covers that\n- No AR remote-repo proxy — plan 2026-05-10-008\n\nPlan: docs/plans/2026-05-11-007-feat-tethysdash-mcps-image-publishing-plan.md\nUnits 1-2. Unit 3 (cut v0.2.0 + smoke) is post-merge operator work.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAps0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAo6wQABro+Wfoo/hVX8vpISVhGUkW\nyIRk4Svvivebqu2buGeh75rugd9jXrzrjKoJoF8FIG/Q0iZaD6vA5tE+trh8D9+r\nKES5KBVBHU4XJ/9vt6NKiloTiR7gL3hXY8kEQ2+YERCJa1NfPTvboetygW9P55Zu\nPw+DKl3gn0lBzWYqsfeF9FFt1jss10mVnrpofsdceviu+dlGzSOVHtqyAdd0lOPr\nejqyOSfthQ1g9GWmyd8LgaocQZGlst4mVnV5gspW/tyN728meFc2QIKWsSCd96J+\nCeMeUzYU7MyvkhyPqsOdGZzkIhijHofLEbI09SOyHIGFWSo3GJLzZpeODnAPe2Jc\nl0HlZbSOsqtkjN3cbu1etSGbD5hvho8Zpfra5ibxNdB134bUqPOved8cnrOvYfSa\nEaYVclglVvtazG0jFK3FEUWddY5E+xRHq6n2lq7m6buz3M984Awan18FlQ+I/13W\nMMamJI8NS7naKceUvHF7/+X9komo7T19k91+JQ4FtpHqAP/hRxu3ZfZggPmJAC9G\nndrFDnqee3f+8gWonVtGNAS3OV4dnZ9H8MeRoUYmUhNPHv+/jEXkyHPO+BMU3TP/\n1evmfo8Gvw/cCrzH2qQMbb7vX/3TpXcTzKGiOnGMNi14uOSE1BIF1e9r+0jYalk9\nhQCkEVN9I2amiQPjcsOq\n=IdaB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-12T03:15:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commit/f2bd383d50785125bc3e1975927bcaee4692969b","node_id":"C_kwDOSajnbNoAKGYyYmQzODNkNTA3ODUxMjViYzNlMTk3NTkyN2JjYWVlNDY5Mjk2OWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commit/67dfb6c1b9c380f21a24c898f0096b196122484a","sha":"67dfb6c1b9c380f21a24c898f0096b196122484a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/67dfb6c1b9c380f21a24c898f0096b196122484a"}],"sha":"f2bd383d50785125bc3e1975927bcaee4692969b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/f2bd383d50785125bc3e1975927bcaee4692969b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43544549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/romer8","id":43544549,"login":"romer8","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQ0NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/67dfb6c1b9c380f21a24c898f0096b196122484a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T03:13:31Z","email":"43544549+romer8@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Gio"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T03:13:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: read runtime plugin registry via HTTP, drop filesystem coupling (#5)\n\nThe standalone now reads the runtime plugin registry from tethysdash\nover HTTP at ${TETHYSDASH_BASE_URL}/runtime-plugins/list/ (a new sibling\nof the existing gated runtime-plugins/sync/ endpoint added on the\ntethysdash side). The filesystem-coupled TETHYSDASH_RUNTIME_REGISTRY_PATH\nenv var is gone -- one less knob, one less footgun, and the standalone\nno longer needs a shared volume with tethysdash to see chatbox-registered\nplugins.\n\n- _load_runtime_plugin_registry_http: new helper that GETs the registry\n  with timeout=5 and allow_redirects=False (defense against tethysdash\n  auth redirects returning HTML 200s). Silent-recovery on any failure\n  (empty BASE_URL, network error, non-200, non-JSON body, non-list\n  payload) — registry-read failures must never crash an unrelated tool\n  call. Failures are logged at warning level.\n\n- _get_all_plugins: routes through the HTTP helper instead of the\n  filesystem loader. Existing tests that patch _get_all_plugins keep\n  working unchanged.\n\n- register_runtime_plugin: feature-flagged off in standalone mode.\n  Returns {\"error\": \"registration_not_supported\", ...} instead of\n  attempting a write. The tool stays in the @mcp.tool surface so\n  chatbox-core''s tool list stays consistent and test_prompts.py''s\n  prompt/tool parity contract holds. Re-enables once auth + a write-\n  side HTTP path land (plan 2026-05-11-004, deferred).\n\n- Deleted tethysdash_mcp/plugin_registry_loader.py — only consumer was\n  the filesystem read that the HTTP helper replaces.\n\n- test_runtime_plugin_registry_http.py: 9 new tests pinning the\n  silent-recovery contract for every failure mode plus the\n  registration_not_supported envelope. test_standalone_independence.py\n  drops the now-deleted module from its inventory.\n\n- Dockerfile comment refreshed (no more \"_RUNTIME_REGISTRY_PATH defaults\n  to /tmp\" since registry isn''t filesystem-coupled anymore).\n\n- README \"Running alongside a local tethysdash dev server\" simplified:\n  Step 3 drops the registry-path export, the \"Registry path must be\n  absolute\" caveat is gone, smoke checklist updates the runtime-plugin-\n  registration step to use the chatbox UI (not the slash command), and\n  the env-var table drops the TETHYSDASH_RUNTIME_REGISTRY_PATH row.\n\n- CHANGELOG documents the architectural shift + the feature-flag.\n\n786 tests pass (was 777; +9 new).\n\nPlan: docs/plans/2026-05-11-006-feat-runtime-plugin-registry-http-endpoint-plan.md\nUnits 2-4. Unit 1 (the tethysdash /runtime-plugins/list/ controller)\nlands in the companion PR on Aquaveo/tethysapp-tethys_dash.","tree":{"sha":"a4d1f32e8c953402b0f4dc705deac3c2947059e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/trees/a4d1f32e8c953402b0f4dc705deac3c2947059e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/commits/67dfb6c1b9c380f21a24c898f0096b196122484a","verification":{"payload":"tree a4d1f32e8c953402b0f4dc705deac3c2947059e2\nparent 718bb50c5bb2a3af045a03f1e9d358ea709236b3\nauthor Gio <43544549+romer8@users.noreply.github.com> 1778555611 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778555611 -0600\n\nfeat: read runtime plugin registry via HTTP, drop filesystem coupling (#5)\n\nThe standalone now reads the runtime plugin registry from tethysdash\nover HTTP at ${TETHYSDASH_BASE_URL}/runtime-plugins/list/ (a new sibling\nof the existing gated runtime-plugins/sync/ endpoint added on the\ntethysdash side). The filesystem-coupled TETHYSDASH_RUNTIME_REGISTRY_PATH\nenv var is gone -- one less knob, one less footgun, and the standalone\nno longer needs a shared volume with tethysdash to see chatbox-registered\nplugins.\n\n- _load_runtime_plugin_registry_http: new helper that GETs the registry\n  with timeout=5 and allow_redirects=False (defense against tethysdash\n  auth redirects returning HTML 200s). Silent-recovery on any failure\n  (empty BASE_URL, network error, non-200, non-JSON body, non-list\n  payload) — registry-read failures must never crash an unrelated tool\n  call. Failures are logged at warning level.\n\n- _get_all_plugins: routes through the HTTP helper instead of the\n  filesystem loader. Existing tests that patch _get_all_plugins keep\n  working unchanged.\n\n- register_runtime_plugin: feature-flagged off in standalone mode.\n  Returns {\"error\": \"registration_not_supported\", ...} instead of\n  attempting a write. The tool stays in the @mcp.tool surface so\n  chatbox-core''s tool list stays consistent and test_prompts.py''s\n  prompt/tool parity contract holds. Re-enables once auth + a write-\n  side HTTP path land (plan 2026-05-11-004, deferred).\n\n- Deleted tethysdash_mcp/plugin_registry_loader.py — only consumer was\n  the filesystem read that the HTTP helper replaces.\n\n- test_runtime_plugin_registry_http.py: 9 new tests pinning the\n  silent-recovery contract for every failure mode plus the\n  registration_not_supported envelope. test_standalone_independence.py\n  drops the now-deleted module from its inventory.\n\n- Dockerfile comment refreshed (no more \"_RUNTIME_REGISTRY_PATH defaults\n  to /tmp\" since registry isn''t filesystem-coupled anymore).\n\n- README \"Running alongside a local tethysdash dev server\" simplified:\n  Step 3 drops the registry-path export, the \"Registry path must be\n  absolute\" caveat is gone, smoke checklist updates the runtime-plugin-\n  registration step to use the chatbox UI (not the slash command), and\n  the env-var table drops the TETHYSDASH_RUNTIME_REGISTRY_PATH row.\n\n- CHANGELOG documents the architectural shift + the feature-flag.\n\n786 tests pass (was 777; +9 new).\n\nPlan: docs/plans/2026-05-11-006-feat-runtime-plugin-registry-http-endpoint-plan.md\nUnits 2-4. Unit 1 (the tethysdash /runtime-plugins/list/ controller)\nlands in the companion PR on Aquaveo/tethysapp-tethys_dash.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAprbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX3MQAHC53UasSyfsmWgr55WIaZDs\npncO4WOK9XQ8m+anhTDrda0xLJS2AWIQihCHzuvjQNPhXvKWQX9EEDbbcCvFcZPg\nhosL0Z/Rzv7zP+yV4VPWTtXWqpAecszly04wzTNA0yKHvhW2m872marm9pCNm5j+\ns90uOHGg+oaOd0/2leaq