a3af045a03f1e9d358ea709236b3"}],"sha":"67dfb6c1b9c380f21a24c898f0096b196122484a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/67dfb6c1b9c380f21a24c898f0096b196122484a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43544549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/romer8","id":43544549,"login":"romer8","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQ0NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/718bb50c5bb2a3af045a03f1e9d358ea709236b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T03:01:32Z","email":"43544549+romer8@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Gio"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T03:01:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: dev runbook + setup-mcp.sh for running alongside tethysdash (#2)\n\n- New \"Running alongside a local tethysdash dev server\" section in README:\n  6-step walkthrough (prerequisites -> tethys dev server -> venv bootstrap\n  -> bridge env vars -> standalone boot -> chatbox URL config -> smoke\n  checklist) with concrete env-var values and known caveats.\n\n- New scripts/setup-mcp.sh modeled on nrds_mcps/scripts/setup-mcp.sh:\n  creates .venv-mcp/, installs tethysdash_mcp/requirements.lock, and runs\n  python -m tethysdash_mcp.mcp_server from the repo dir so the package\n  resolves without a pyproject.toml. Subcommands: --setup, --run, no-arg.\n  Honors MCP_PORT, MCP_HOST, MCP_TRANSPORT, TETHYSDASH_BASE_URL,\n  TETHYSDASH_RUNTIME_REGISTRY_PATH, ALLOWED_ORIGINS from the environment.\n\n- Quick Start (Python) section rewritten to use the new script.\n\n- Development section updated to run pytest via the script-managed venv.\n\n- .gitignore excludes .venv-mcp/.\n\n- CHANGELOG captures the script + CLI smoke evidence: /health 200,\n  list_tools returns 25, create_card returns a clean envelope,\n  list_intake_plugins returns a structured error envelope against an\n  unreachable backend, input-validation middleware catches wrong kwargs\n  with a rich envelope. Browser-side chatbox flows (LLM tool selection,\n  runtime-plugin registration via TETHYSDASH_RUNTIME_REGISTRY_PATH bridge,\n  patch_visualization round-trip) noted as pending human follow-up.\n\n- Gotcha caught + fixed mid-smoke: python -m tethysdash_mcp.mcp_server\n  needs cwd to contain the package directory (no pyproject.toml). The\n  script handles this internally via cd \"$PROJECT_DIR\" before exec.\n\nPlan reference: docs/plans/2026-05-11-005-feat-tethysdash-mcps-dev-runbook-plan.md\nSatisfies plan 003 revival triggers 1 and 3; trigger 2 pending browser smoke.","tree":{"sha":"36e259f46725e0d0729b1ea0b79fee54af786ba7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/trees/36e259f46725e0d0729b1ea0b79fee54af786ba7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/commits/718bb50c5bb2a3af045a03f1e9d358ea709236b3","verification":{"payload":"tree 36e259f46725e0d0729b1ea0b79fee54af786ba7\nparent b9848b4d11de46769d8ea4dec30cbe9165651740\nauthor Gio <43544549+romer8@users.noreply.github.com> 1778554892 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778554892 -0600\n\nfeat: dev runbook + setup-mcp.sh for running alongside tethysdash (#2)\n\n- New \"Running alongside a local tethysdash dev server\" section in README:\n  6-step walkthrough (prerequisites -> tethys dev server -> venv bootstrap\n  -> bridge env vars -> standalone boot -> chatbox URL config -> smoke\n  checklist) with concrete env-var values and known caveats.\n\n- New scripts/setup-mcp.sh modeled on nrds_mcps/scripts/setup-mcp.sh:\n  creates .venv-mcp/, installs tethysdash_mcp/requirements.lock, and runs\n  python -m tethysdash_mcp.mcp_server from the repo dir so the package\n  resolves without a pyproject.toml. Subcommands: --setup, --run, no-arg.\n  Honors MCP_PORT, MCP_HOST, MCP_TRANSPORT, TETHYSDASH_BASE_URL,\n  TETHYSDASH_RUNTIME_REGISTRY_PATH, ALLOWED_ORIGINS from the environment.\n\n- Quick Start (Python) section rewritten to use the new script.\n\n- Development section updated to run pytest via the script-managed venv.\n\n- .gitignore excludes .venv-mcp/.\n\n- CHANGELOG captures the script + CLI smoke evidence: /health 200,\n  list_tools returns 25, create_card returns a clean envelope,\n  list_intake_plugins returns a structured error envelope against an\n  unreachable backend, input-validation middleware catches wrong kwargs\n  with a rich envelope. Browser-side chatbox flows (LLM tool selection,\n  runtime-plugin registration via TETHYSDASH_RUNTIME_REGISTRY_PATH bridge,\n  patch_visualization round-trip) noted as pending human follow-up.\n\n- Gotcha caught + fixed mid-smoke: python -m tethysdash_mcp.mcp_server\n  needs cwd to contain the package directory (no pyproject.toml). The\n  script handles this internally via cd \"$PROJECT_DIR\" before exec.\n\nPlan reference: docs/plans/2026-05-11-005-feat-tethysdash-mcps-dev-runbook-plan.md\nSatisfies plan 003 revival triggers 1 and 3; trigger 2 pending browser smoke.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqApgMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA4EQABKYT3vHXJ91qGwIapq1Zigq\nQOxxT/3XO+xQqU/e56biCvuQ/pzc20DLeJBgr0uJvzdUAIP/psKzIMRs10bakGNJ\nwJxsBLR1GfD/jBTNZW7K8IBUaVgNxPbVAnsKQuGHgXtQk5dnN8rtc+MafwiE6kT9\nwRGJgANrI2J8LbjX4yIi0