6769d8ea4dec30cbe9165651740"}],"sha":"718bb50c5bb2a3af045a03f1e9d358ea709236b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/718bb50c5bb2a3af045a03f1e9d358ea709236b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43544549?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/romer8","id":43544549,"login":"romer8","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQ0NTQ5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romer8","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/commits/b9848b4d11de46769d8ea4dec30cbe9165651740/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T17:36:02Z","email":"43544549+romer8@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Gio"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T17:36:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: initial standalone extract of the tethysdash MCP server (#1)\n\nCode-only duplicate of tethysapp-tethys_dash/tethysapp/tethysdash/mcp/.\nThe embedded server stays the developer-local default; this repo is the\ndeploy-ready artifact (container, no Django, no Tethys stack).\n\nSurface: 25 @mcp.tool + 25 @mcp.prompt definitions (parity with the\nembedded server as of the source commit). FastMCP Streamable HTTP at\n/mcp with /sse compat path and a /health liveness probe.\n\nStandalone-specific rewrites vs the embedded source:\n- All `from tethysapp.tethysdash.*` imports rewritten to\n  `from tethysdash_mcp.*`.\n- plugin_helpers.py shipped as a symbol-allowlist copy (omits the\n  TethysDashPlugin base class, send_websocket_message, and\n  validate_feature_collection to avoid the intake.source.base /\n  Django Channels coupling).\n- editable_schemas.py loads the editableSchemas.json whitelist from a\n  package-local data/ directory rather than walking out to the React\n  frontend tree.\n- plugin_registry_loader._RUNTIME_REGISTRY_PATH reads\n  TETHYSDASH_RUNTIME_REGISTRY_PATH (default /tmp/runtimePluginRegistry.json)\n  rather than the embedded reactapp/generated/ path.\n- TETHYSDASH_BASE_URL defaults to \"\" so an unconfigured deployment\n  surfaces a structured backend_not_configured envelope rather than\n  silently mis-targeting localhost:8080.\n- Entry-point env vars: MCP_PORT (was TETHYSDASH_MCP_PORT, default 9000),\n  MCP_HOST package default 127.0.0.1, ALLOWED_ORIGINS unset -> wildcard.\n- Dockerfile ENV overrides MCP_HOST to 0.0.0.0 so the published port is\n  reachable inside the container.\n\nTests (777 passing, ~6s in a clean venv):\n- All 14 contract suites from the embedded server (visualization +\n  layer + patch + prompt + transport/CORS contracts) ported with imports\n  rewritten.\n- test_standalone_independence.py guards that no `tethysapp.*` or\n  `django` modules load during import -- runs in a subprocess so it\n  doesn''t pollute other tests by popping sys.modules.\n- A conftest fixture sets TETHYSDASH_BASE_URL to a sentinel so the\n  backend-not-configured guard does not short-circuit mocked HTTP tests.\n\nCI (.github/workflows/ci.yml): smoke import + standalone-independence +\nfull pytest run, then docker build with a /health-probe smoke. No push,\nno release pipeline -- those land in a separate plan when deploy work\nresumes.\n\nDockerfile: two-stage builder -> runtime, non-root mcp user, HOME=/tmp\nfor read-only-fs safety, /health HEALTHCHECK, entrypoint\n`python -m tethysdash_mcp.mcp_server`.","tree":{"sha":"ebfd6565c568c4417eaa7a365204dafee04447d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/trees/ebfd6565c568c4417eaa7a365204dafee04447d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Aquaveo/tethysdash_mcps/git/commits/b9848b4d11de46769d8ea4dec30cbe9165651740","verification":{"payload":"tree ebfd6565c568c4417eaa7a365204dafee04447d9\nparent b98eda469dd5307b922e7729358e467c53bf124e\nauthor Gio <43544549+romer8@users.noreply.github.com> 1778520962 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778520962 -0600\n\nfeat: initial standalone extract of the tethysdash MCP server (#1)\n\nCode-only duplicate of tethysapp-tethys_dash/tethysapp/tethysdash/mcp/.\nThe embedded server stays the developer-local default; this repo is the\ndeploy-ready artifact (container, no Django, no Tethys stack).\n\nSurface: 25 @mcp.tool + 25 @mcp.prompt definitions (parity with the\nembedded server as of the source commit). FastMCP Streamable HTTP at\n/mcp with /sse compat path and a /health liveness probe.\n\nStandalone-specific rewrites vs the embedded source:\n- All `from tethysapp.tethysdash.*` imports rewritten to\n  `from tethysdash_mcp.*`.\n- plugin_helpers.py shipped as a symbol-allowlist copy (omits the\n  TethysDashPlugin base class, send_websocket_message, and\n  validate_feature_collection to avoid the intake.source.base /\n  Django Channels coupling).\n- editable_schemas.py loads the editableSchemas.json whitelist from a\n  package-local data/ directory rather than walking out to the React\n  frontend tree.\n- plugin_registry_loader._RUNTIME_REGISTRY_PATH reads\n  TETHYSDASH_RUNTIME_REGISTRY_PATH (default /tmp/runtimePluginRegistry.json)\n  rather than the embedded reactapp/generated/ path.\n- TETHYSDASH_BASE_URL defaults to \"\" so an unconfigured deployment\n  surfaces a structured backend_not_configured envelope rather than\n  silently mis-targeting localhost:8080.\n- Entry-point env vars: MCP_PORT (was TETHYSDASH_MCP_PORT, default 9000),\n  MCP_HOST package default 127.0.0.1, ALLOWED_ORIGINS unset -> wildcard.\n- Dockerfile ENV overrides MCP_HOST to 0.0.0.0 so the published port is\n  reachable inside the container.\n\nTests (777 passing, ~6s in a clean venv):\n- All 14 contract suites from the embedded server (visualization +\n  layer + patch + prompt + transport/CORS contracts) ported with imports\n  rewritten.\n- test_standalone_independence.py guards that no `tethysapp.*` or\n  `django` modules load during import -- runs in a subprocess so it\n  doesn''t pollute other tests by popping sys.modules.\n- A conftest fixture sets TETHYSDASH_BASE_URL to a sentinel so the\n  backend-not-configured guard does not short-circuit mocked HTTP tests.\n\nCI (.github/workflows/ci.yml): smoke import + standalone-independence +\nfull pytest run, then docker build with a /health-probe smoke. No push,\nno release pipeline -- those land in a separate plan when deploy work\nresumes.\n\nDockerfile: two-stage builder -> runtime, non-root mcp user, HOME=/tmp\nfor read-only-fs safety, /health HEALTHCHECK, entrypoint\n`python -m tethysdash_mcp.mcp_server`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAhOCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAk4oQAIKEZCEDCexlBa8CyUqOxtZA\nR/M9t8Lkpv9pJWYmXtChBR9+qjmd9xREaeS59eeo1QZPZoCLMmDYlPeDQBnkHFB0\n5Rb9zONlSH/Xqs4aPPzeSjUOT4s/bxvWN0b6GdAwGBHsXrInL9HAuaJLKGnnRhnM\nvV60/bW7wmchFfyOzNjdPeR1DrW6yC2innI6RKGndmWhRmSyYvxp6PjyBUz3UeFO\n0nE1+hz2Lxv6gEl3vywCruhJj1h7jZvpLACdco3nb9FqlmlnGCAgXNF8WsBNh+kS\n8AoLIApjhbI2iAfnu41Q5+sWto/TwYaDObbHRcKfTfUZaeoEM4M+fCsAH4K51Zak\n/cUpV1Q0t6CvVOgTL73xpdqWYEH8F/dRovT0mvf1RIsB4j90fjnRXGvYnFtShiJz\nDoy/8xU/2rVnoqmXF2R4EoTP4chcBGdCNyf14zyiranr0at7WBReiA/Etvg+W2TC\nTbHUWaUa+R0pNRTdgxjpbPbgvcZ4+QwFpJo5PbrcbdvEv5HFGUHaLAHenh2//d8T\n76xCRQWSpr8ICNLs0LuTreg3T6zA5O6e9brlPTNlqmYhy/MXRhC5O+xQ+MX8mAPJ\n0+kU97BGDJ1Q0sz/HbMVVV6NmSJ+IRojKRbp8Pm62PTWzbNEqckPYyxDllWOU1BQ\nBX1zvoFn22M/bgZcG036\n=OOBx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,