om/users/rajeshuriti","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rajeshuriti/claude-terminology/commit/7dd9f3ca0b2c1ed21446ca94345818272d7f36c1","node_id":"C_kwDOSan7iNoAKDdkZDlmM2NhMGIyYzFlZDIxNDQ2Y2E5NDM0NTgxODI3MmQ3ZjM2YzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rajeshuriti/claude-terminology/commit/4cbb35935abaf6adde6aba4d3abf35fbe401d455","sha":"4cbb35935abaf6adde6aba4d3abf35fbe401d455","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rajeshuriti/claude-terminology/commits/4cbb35935abaf6adde6aba4d3abf35fbe401d455"}],"sha":"7dd9f3ca0b2c1ed21446ca94345818272d7f36c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rajeshuriti/claude-terminology/commits/7dd9f3ca0b2c1ed21446ca94345818272d7f36c1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11350143?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rajeshuriti","id":11350143,"login":"rajeshuriti","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzUwMTQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rajeshuriti/claude-terminology/commits/4cbb35935abaf6adde6aba4d3abf35fbe401d455/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-12T01:49:44Z","email":"rajeshuriti@gmail.com","name":"Rajesh Uriti"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-12T01:49:44Z","email":"rajeshuriti@gmail.com","name":"Rajesh Uriti"},"message":"Add Certification Practice Exam — 30 interactive scenario-based questions\n\nFull interactive quiz for Claude Certified Architect – Foundations prep.\n\nSCREENS:\n1. Intro Screen: domain selection grid (All + 8 domains), exam overview\n   (30 questions, 8 domains, 45-60 min, Advanced), exam philosophy box,\n   domain-filtered question counts, animated Start button\n2. Quiz Screen (per question):\n   - Scenario badge + domain badge at top\n   - Animated progress bar\n   - Question card with 4 option buttons\n   - On selection: correct (emerald) / wrong (rose) / dimmed (others)\n   - Verdict banner with correct answer revealed\n   - Expandable explanation accordion with:\n     - Why the correct answer is right (detailed technical explanation)\n     - Why each wrong answer fails (individual rebuttals)\n     - Exam Takeaway box (sky blue highlight)\n     - Reference link\n   - Next / View Results navigation\n3. Results Screen:\n   - Animated SVG score ring with % and pass/fail indicator\n   - Passing threshold display (72%)\n   - Domain radar chart (performance across all 8 domains)\n   - Domain bar chart (colored red if <70%, domain color if ≥70%)\n   - Retry / Change Domain action buttons\n   - Question review panel with wrong/correct/all filter\n   - Per-question expandable review with options + takeaway\n\nDATA (certificationQuizData.ts):\n- 30 questions across 8 domains: Schema Design, Batch Processing,\n  Tool Design, MCP Security, Error Handling, Agentic Architecture,\n  Context Management, Output Validation\n- Each question: scenario label, domain, difficulty, 4 options,\n  correctIndex, detailed explanation (often multi-paragraph with\n  concrete examples), whyOthersWrong array, examTakeaway, reference\n- All 30 questions from the official exam prep guide\n\nSIDEBAR: 🏆 Cert Practice Exam (amber-orange gradient, NEW badge)\nROUTE: /certification\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"