dde6aba4d3abf35fbe401d455"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11350143?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rajeshuriti","id":11350143,"login":"rajeshuriti","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzUwMTQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rajeshuriti/claude-terminology/commits/e194c4ca9207ef1ac05e27a290653ca9a625e581/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T21:31:41Z","email":"rajeshuriti@gmail.com","name":"Rajesh Uriti"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T21:31:41Z","email":"rajeshuriti@gmail.com","name":"Rajesh Uriti"},"message":"Add Slash Commands Studio — interactive command learning system\n\nNew /commands route with 14-section visual command mastery platform.\n\nHighlights:\n- Command Overview: searchable/filterable grid of all 24 Claude Code commands,\n  with category chips, risk badges, token impact, and inline detail panel\n  showing purpose / state changes / workflow tabs per command\n- Interactive Playground: live terminal simulator — type /compact, /agents, /plan,\n  etc. and watch session state change in real-time (token bar, model, agent count,\n  cost, background tasks). Tab autocomplete, command history, radar chart of\n  session health. Reset to baseline anytime.\n- Command Chaining: 5 pre-built workflow chains (Refactor, Feature, Debug,\n  Multi-Agent, Onboarding) with animated step-by-step pipeline visualization\n  and \"why order matters\" explanation per chain\n- Workflow Templates: 6 pro workflow templates with step-by-step sequences,\n  use-case descriptions, estimated time, and command notes per step\n- Category Sections: Session, Context & Memory, Planning, Agents, MCP, Review/Debug,\n  Automation — each with bar chart of token impact and detail panel per command\n- Relationship Graph: ReactFlow graph showing command-to-command chains with\n  animated edges for strong relationships, click-to-inspect node detail panel\n- Anti-Patterns: expandable severity-coded cards for every documented misuse\n  pattern across all commands, with fix for each\n\nData model (slashCommandsData.ts):\n- 24 slash commands with: syntax, category, difficulty, riskLevel, tokenImpact,\n  sideEffects, compatibleWith, unsafePatterns, stateChanges, workflowUsage,\n  realWorldScenario, internalNote\n- 12 command chains for the relationship graph\n- 6 workflow templates with step-by-step command sequences\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"41500f3555933144612a1f45359bdfb803bcbf97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rajeshuriti/claude-terminology/git/trees/41500f3555933144612a1f45359bdfb803bcbf97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rajeshuriti/claude-terminology/git/commits/e194c4ca9207ef1ac05e27a290653ca9a625e581","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11350143?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rajeshuriti","id":11350143,"login":"rajeshuriti","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzUwMTQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rajeshuriti/claude-terminology/commit/e194c4ca9207ef1ac05e27a290653ca9a625e581","node_id":"C_kwDOSan7iNoAKGUxOTRjNGNhOTIwN2VmMWFjMDVlMjdhMjkwNjUzY2E5YTYyNWU1ODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rajeshuriti/claude-terminology/commit/54c3cf6355c7b162f89b31ccded733ae11a27ffb","sha":"54c3cf6355c7b162f89b31ccded733ae11a27ffb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rajeshuriti/claude-terminology/commits/54c3cf6355c7b162f89b31ccded733ae11a27ffb"}],"sha":"e194c4ca9207ef1ac05e27a290653ca9a625e581","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rajeshuriti/claude-terminology/commits/e194c4ca9207ef1ac05e27a290653ca9a625e581"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11350143?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rajeshuriti","id":11350143,"login":"rajeshuriti","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzUwMTQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rajeshuriti/claude-terminology/commits/54c3cf6355c7b162f89b31ccded733ae11a27ffb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-11T20:57:28Z","email":"rajeshuriti@gmail.com","name":"Rajesh Uriti"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-11T20:57:28Z","email":"rajeshuriti@gmail.com","name":"Rajesh Uriti"},"message":"Add Claude Internals interactive learning section\n\nNew /internals route with 14-section educational platform covering every\nClaude configuration file and runtime concept. Full secondary sidebar\nnavigation with progress tracking.\n\nSections:\n- Architecture Overview: clickable animated pipeline (User→System→CLAUDE.md→\n  Config→Tools→Memory→Model→Response) with node detail panel\n- Execution Flow: 10-step animated timeline with replay button, expandable\n  technical details, and layer distribution chart\n- CLAUDE.md Explorer: tabbed syntax/good-example/anti-pattern/tips with\n  CodeBlock copy button, priority stack visualizer, mistake list\n- Settings/Config: claude.json deep dive with permission patterns\n- System Prompts: authority hierarchy, API usage, anti-patterns\n- Prompt Layers: interactive 7-layer priority stack with hide/show toggles,\n  conflict resolution rules, layer detail on click\n- Tool Calling: animated 7-step pipeline, tool_choice comparison table,\n  critical insights, schema example\n- Memory & Context: Recharts horizontal bar token budget breakdown,\n  memory types, overflow strategy comparison (truncation/summarization/RAG)\n- MCP Integration: architecture diagram, real-world server examples,\n  config code block, security warning\n- Hooks & Automation: event types, auto-lint example config, best practices\n- Permissions: pattern examples, 3-tier level breakdown, danger list\n- Common Mistakes: 8 expandable cards with severity (critical/high/medium),\n  why-it-fails + fix for each\n- Best Practices: filterable grid by category with impact/effort ratings\n- Comparisons: 3 side-by-side tables (CLAUDE.md vs json, System vs User,\n  MCP vs Tool Use)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8cbefa59665ac2f6cde7c487e4738dc4f9de6d1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rajeshuriti/claude-terminology/git/trees/8cbefa59665ac2f6cde7c487e4738dc4f9de6d1b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rajeshuriti/claude-terminology/git/commits/54c3cf6355c7b162f89b31ccded733ae11a27ffb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11350143?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rajeshuriti","id":11350143,"login":"rajeshuriti","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMzUwMTQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajeshuriti","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rajeshuriti/claude-terminology/commit/54c3cf6355c7b162f89b31ccded733ae11a27ffb","node_id":"C_kwDOSan7iNoAKDU0YzNjZjYzNTVjN2IxNjJmODliMzFjY2RlZDczM2FlMTFhMjdmZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://gi